  values ((select id from public.learning_units where release_id = v_release_id and source_key = '06_Domain_2_Hub_Information_Giving'), 'static-html', 'legacy_static_html', 0, jsonb_build_object('html', '

<header>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="topbar">
      
      <span>The CASC Academy · by MedLex Foundations</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tagrow">
      <span class="tag prime">Domain 2 of 8</span>
      <span class="tag">Information Giving &amp; Medication Conversations</span>
      <span class="tag">8 constructs · knowledge under load</span>
    </div>
    <h1>Information Giving</h1>
    <p class="sub">Candidates call these the &ldquo;easy&rdquo; stations — <em>just explain lithium, just describe the diagnosis</em>. Examiners mark the other end of the conversation: not what you said, but what a frightened person <b style="color:var(--lgold)">left able to use</b>. Your pharmacology is assumed — it is the entry ticket, not the prize. This domain trains the harder thing: delivering knowledge so that it lands, and stays.</p>
    <div class="lens"><b>THE LENS, APPLIED TO THIS DOMAIN</b>
      &ldquo;Would I trust this candidate as my registrar?&rdquo; — In this domain the evidence is simple: would my patients leave this doctor''s clinic knowing what keeps them safe — and would they come back?</div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ============ 1 WHY FIRST ============ -->
<section id="s1">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">01</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">Why this domain comes first</span>
    <h2>The station is not about the drug</h2>
    <p class="intro">Every year, candidates walk out of information-giving stations feeling excellent — they covered the mechanism, the side-effects, the monitoring, everything. And the mark disappoints them, because the examiner was never counting facts. They were watching the patient: did she understand? Did her fear get answered, or lectured past? Could she repeat the one thing that keeps her safe? The drug is the disguise; <b>the conversation is the station</b>. That reframe — from telling to landing — is what this domain installs.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>What this domain assumes, and what it doesn''t:</b> it assumes you know the drugs — doses, interactions, monitoring schedules live in your textbooks, not here. What it trains is everything the textbook cannot: opening with their agenda, chunking, plain words, answering the fear inside the question, landing the safety-critical content conversationally, and proving it landed. Domain 1 built the rapport; this domain spends it.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 2 THE CONSTRUCTS ============ -->
<section id="s2">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">02</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">Your mastery spine for this domain</span>
    <h2>The eight skills examiners are marking</h2>
    <p class="intro">These are the domain''s constructs — the specific, checkable skills behind the information-giving marks. As you work through the Academy, each one climbs the ladder you met in the orientation: Explored → Recognised → Demonstrated → Validated. This spine fills as you work, and it is the honest answer to &ldquo;am I ready?&rdquo;</p>
    <div class="spine">
      <div class="spine-head"><b>Information Giving &amp; Medication Conversations</b><span>0 of 8 recognised — your spine starts here</span></div>
      <div class="cons">
        <div class="con"><span class="n">1</span><span>The agenda-first opening — what they already know, and what they came to ask</span><span class="dots"><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i></span></div>
        <div class="con"><span class="n">2</span><span>Chunk and check — information in small pieces, each landing confirmed</span><span class="dots"><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i></span></div>
        <div class="con"><span class="n">3</span><span>Plain words for clinical facts — language calibrated to the person in the chair</span><span class="dots"><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i></span></div>
        <div class="con"><span class="n">4</span><span>Responding to concerns, not reciting facts — the fear inside the question, answered</span><span class="dots"><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i></span></div>
        <div class="con"><span class="n">5</span><span>The non-negotiables — safety-critical content delivered conversationally, never lost</span><span class="dots"><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i></span></div>
        <div class="con"><span class="n">6</span><span>The hard question — honesty without false reassurance</span><span class="dots"><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i></span></div>
        <div class="con"><span class="n">7</span><span>Prioritising when time is short — the must-say versus the leaflet</span><span class="dots"><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i></span></div>
        <div class="con"><span class="n">8</span><span>Teach-back — proving the information landed before they leave</span><span class="dots"><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i><i class="dot"></i></span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="legend">
        <span><i></i> Explored</span><span><i></i> Recognised</span><span><i></i> Demonstrated</span><span><i></i> Validated</span>
        <span class="f"><i></i> = achieved</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 3 STATIONS ============ -->
<section id="s3">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">03</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">The stations in this domain</span>
    <h2>Walk them in order</h2>
    <div class="stn">
      <div class="srow" style="cursor:pointer">
        <span class="num">2.1</span>
        <span class="t"><b>Starting Lithium</b><span>Nadia, newly diagnosed, ready to begin a drug with real dangers. The domain''s opening: constructs 1–3 and 5 — and the safety content that must survive the conversation.</span></span>
        <span class="chip go">Begin here</span>
      </div>
      <div class="srow" style="cursor:pointer">
        <span class="num">2.2</span>
        <span class="t"><b>The Clozapine Conversation</b><span>Marcus, two antipsychotics down, one option left — hope and hazard in the same molecule. Construct 6 under real load: honesty without false reassurance.</span></span>
        <span class="chip">Station 2</span>
      </div>
      <div class="srow" style="cursor:pointer">
        <span class="num">2.3</span>
        <span class="t"><b>&ldquo;What Does Schizophrenia Mean, Doctor?&rdquo;</b><span>A new diagnosis, and a word that arrives carrying everything the films ever put in it. Construct 4 — answering what the word means to <em>them</em>.</span></span>
        <span class="chip">Station 3</span>
      </div>
      <div class="srow" style="cursor:pointer">
        <span class="num">2.4</span>
        <span class="t"><b>ECT, Explained</b><span>The treatment with a reputation. Information and consent living in the same conversation — where this domain shakes hands with capacity and the law.</span></span>
        <span class="chip">Station 4</span>
      </div>
      <div class="srow" style="cursor:pointer">
        <span class="num">2.5</span>
        <span class="t"><b>Antidepressants in Pregnancy</b><span>Two patients, one decision, and no verdicts to hand down — a balanced-risk conversation that ends in her informed choice, not yours.</span></span>
        <span class="chip">Station 5</span>
      </div>
      <div class="srow" style="cursor:pointer">
        <span class="num">2.6</span>
        <span class="t"><b>Panic Disorder and Explaining CBT</b><span>The difference between a leaflet and a lightbulb — a vicious cycle built out of her own Tuesday, with the last link left open until she closes it herself.</span></span>
        <span class="chip">Station 6</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="also"><b>And it is tested again under fire.</b> The lithium-toxicity emergency call and the breaking-bad-news station both carry these constructs into harder weather — information delivered while everything urgent is happening. What you build here is what holds there.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 4 ENTRY DECISION ============ -->
<section id="s4">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">04</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">Before you enter</span>
    <h2>One decision at the door</h2>
    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>What is an information-giving station marked on?</h3>
      <p class="stem">Two candidates explain the same drug, accurately, in the same seven minutes. One scores clearly higher. What most likely made the difference?</p>
      <p class="hint">Choose an answer. If it''s not the best one, you can try again.</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">They covered more of the topic — mechanism, side-effects, monitoring — within the seven minutes.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="1">They explained with greater fluency and command, showing the examiner real depth of knowledge.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="2">Their patient could repeat back the things that keep her safe — the examiner watched it land.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="0-0"><b>THE EXAMINER''S VIEW</b>Coverage is not the currency. A complete lecture nobody absorbed marks as a lecture — the examiner was watching her face while you covered things. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="0-1"><b>THE EXAMINER''S VIEW</b>Fluency impresses colleagues. Frightened patients don''t need a command performance; they need small pieces, plain words, and their actual fear answered. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>Information-giving is marked at the receiving end. What landed, what she can repeat, whether she would come back — everything in this domain aims at that. The drug is the disguise; the conversation is the station.</template>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ DONE ============ -->
<section class="done on-navy" id="s5">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow gold">Domain open</span>
    <h2>What did she leave knowing? Prove it.</h2>
    <p>Station 2.1 is a drug conversation every candidate can recite. The marks are in what Nadia leaves able to use — and after it, you will never &ldquo;cover the side-effects&rdquo; again.</p>
    <a class="btn mark" href="07_Station_2.1_Starting_Lithium.html">Begin Station 2.1 · Starting Lithium</a>
    <div class="tag2">Where Medicine Meets Justice</div>
  </div>
</section>

<footer><div class="wrap">
  <span>The CASC Academy · by MedLex Foundations</span>
  <span>Domain 2 · Information Giving &amp; Medication Conversations</span>
</div></footer>


