<header>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="topbar">
      
      <span>The CASC Academy · by MedLex Foundations</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tagrow">
      <span class="tag prime">Station 5.2 · Domain 5</span>
      <span class="tag">Capacity, Consent &amp; the Law</span><span class="tag">Management &amp; Emergency</span>
      <span class="tag">General Adult</span><span class="tag">Discharge · Holding powers</span>
    </div>
    <h1>&ldquo;I&rsquo;m Leaving&rdquo;</h1>
    <p class="sub">Terry, 34, a forklift driver, was admitted informally six days ago with a severe depressive episode after his marriage ended. He has been improving. Tonight he is at the nurses&rsquo; station with his coat on and a holdall at his feet: &ldquo;I&rsquo;m informal, right? That&rsquo;s what informal means. I&rsquo;m telling you, not asking you.&rdquo; The nurse&rsquo;s eyes find yours. No section, no seclusion, no order to point to &mdash; a man with every legal right to walk out, unless the next few minutes find a reason he cannot. Station 5.1 ran the statutory test seated, at a bedside, with time. This is the same test standing up, in a corridor, in minutes &mdash; capacity and risk, assessed at a door. <b>The door is not the emergency. The argument is.</b></p>
    <div class="lens"><b>THE QUESTION BEHIND EVERY MARK</b>
      &ldquo;Would I be confident to have this candidate as my registrar?&rdquo; At this door it sharpens: if my registrar meets a coat at the nurses&rsquo; station, do I get back capacity and risk assessed in minutes &mdash; the reason found, the test run by name, tonight&rsquo;s dangers weighed &mdash; and an honest decision either way: a leaving made safe, or a holding power used openly? Or do I get a corridor negotiation that ends with security called, a signature on a form, and nothing assessed at all?</div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="modebar"><div class="wrap">
  <span class="label">MODE</span>
  <div class="mtoggle">
    <button id="mLearn" class="active">Learn Mode</button>
    <button id="mExam">Exam Mode</button>
  </div>
  <span class="timer" id="timer">07:00</span>
  <div class="bar"><i id="bar"></i></div><span class="pct" id="pct">0%</span>
</div></div>

<div id="learnPanel">

<!-- ============ 1 WHY THIS STATION EXISTS ============ -->
<section id="s1">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">01</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">Why this station exists</span>
    <h2>What the examiners built this to find out</h2>
    <p class="intro">Every ward has this evening, and the exam builds it because it compresses the whole domain into minutes. Four things carry the marks. <b>De-escalation by assessment:</b> you walk with him, not in front of him &mdash; and the first real question is &ldquo;why tonight?&rdquo;, because almost every leaving has a trigger, many triggers are solvable, and the reason is also evidence for the weighing. <b>The same statutory test, standing up:</b> capacity for THIS decision &mdash; leaving now &mdash; run quickly but by name: understands what leaving means, retains it, weighs it, communicates it, with the impairment question alongside. <b>Tonight&rsquo;s risk, freshly assessed:</b> not the admission&rsquo;s risk &mdash; this evening&rsquo;s: mood now, thoughts now, and the question that decides everything &mdash; what happens after the door? And <b>the honest fork:</b> capacity intact and risk manageable means the right to leave, made as safe as planning can make it &mdash; no promises extracted; illness driving the decision, or risk unmet, means the holding powers every system provides &mdash; used openly at the end, never brandished at the start.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>What makes it hard:</b> two pulls, and both feel like good doctoring. Toward the argument &mdash; persuade, bargain, block the doorway, hold the section over him like weather: the refusal of his leaving, mounted with real concern, while nothing is assessed and the corridor fills. And toward the open door &mdash; &ldquo;he&rsquo;s informal, it&rsquo;s his right&rdquo;: the rubber stamp from 5.1 wearing discharge paperwork, a signature collected where an assessment should have been. Notice both pulls in the decisions below. We will come back to them.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 2 THREE TAKES ============ -->
<section id="s2">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">02</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">The station, three ways</span>
    <h2>Two ways to fail. One way to pass.</h2>
    <p class="intro">One failure fights the leaving. The other waves it through. Tap the gold circles for the examiner&rsquo;s thinking at each moment.</p>

    <div class="player">
      <div class="player-head">
        <span class="who"><b>Station 5.2</b> · The informal patient leaving · capacity &amp; risk · 7 minutes</span>
        <div class="toggle">
          <button class="active" data-t="a">Fail 1 · The argument</button>
          <button data-t="b">Fail 2 · The open door</button>
          <button data-t="c">The pass</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="script" id="tk-a">
        <p class="takenote"><b>FAIL 1 — THE ARGUMENT.</b> Concern converted into obstruction &mdash; persuasion, bargaining, and finally the section held over him like weather. Watch the corridor fill while nothing gets assessed.</p>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Terry</span><span class="txt"><em>(coat on, holdall at his feet, jaw set)</em> I&rsquo;m informal, right? That&rsquo;s what the word means &mdash; I came in on my own two feet and I can leave on them. So I&rsquo;m telling you, not asking you: I&rsquo;m going home. Tonight.</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt">Terry, stop &mdash; just stop for a second. You were admitted six days ago because things were very serious, and you are not well enough for this. Walking out at nine o&rsquo;clock at night helps nobody. Go back to the day room, and we can talk about discharge properly at the ward round tomorrow. That&rsquo;s the sensible way to do this.</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>&ldquo;Stop&rdquo; &mdash; the first word is a blockade, and every sentence after it is a verdict: &ldquo;not well enough&rdquo; declared with nothing assessed, tonight&rsquo;s leaving refused by a doctor with no legal power to refuse it. The one question that would actually open this station &mdash; <em>why tonight?</em> &mdash; has not been asked. He came to the nurses&rsquo; station with a decision; he is being handed a curfew.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Terry</span><span class="txt"><em>(voice rising)</em> Sensible? You want to talk to me about sensible? I&rsquo;ve got a reason to be home and none of you have asked me what it is. I&rsquo;m not a prisoner. Get out of my way.</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt">I&rsquo;m not in your way &mdash; but I&rsquo;ll be honest with you: if you try to walk out of that door tonight, I will have no choice but to put you on a section. Is that what you want? Because that&rsquo;s where this is heading. Don&rsquo;t make me do that, Terry.</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>The section as leverage &mdash; the single worst sentence available at this door. Detention is an assessment&rsquo;s conclusion, never a threat&rsquo;s content; brandished like this it is coercion of an informal patient, it poisons every future admission he might ever agree to, and &mdash; note the emptiness &mdash; it is a threat made INSTEAD of the assessment that could tell anyone whether any power even applies.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt"><em>(to the nurse, reaching for the phone)</em> Can you get security up here, please &mdash; and I&rsquo;ll document that he&rsquo;s agitated and threatening to abscond. <em>(Terry, who was never once asked a question, is now shouting in a corridor &mdash; frightened, cornered, and further from safety than when he put his coat on)</em></span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>&ldquo;Agitated&rdquo; &mdash; a finding this corridor manufactured, about to be documented as his property. An informal patient cannot &ldquo;abscond&rdquo;; the word itself has quietly detained him. Total assessment conducted: none. Capacity: untested. Tonight&rsquo;s risk: unasked. The reason he needed to be home: still unknown &mdash; and now unknowable, because the alliance just died in front of security.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="script" id="tk-b" style="display:none">
        <p class="takenote"><b>FAIL 2 — THE OPEN DOOR.</b> The rubber stamp with discharge paperwork: &ldquo;he&rsquo;s informal, it&rsquo;s his right&rdquo; &mdash; a signature collected where an assessment should have been.</p>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Terry</span><span class="txt"><em>(coat on, holdall at his feet, jaw set)</em> I&rsquo;m informal, right? That&rsquo;s what the word means &mdash; I came in on my own two feet and I can leave on them. So I&rsquo;m telling you, not asking you: I&rsquo;m going home. Tonight.</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt">You&rsquo;re right, Terry &mdash; you&rsquo;re here informally, and that means I can&rsquo;t stop you. I wouldn&rsquo;t try. Let me get the self-discharge form so we can do this properly, and I&rsquo;ll make sure the pharmacy sends your medication after you.</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>Every word is technically true &mdash; and it is 5.1&rsquo;s rubber stamp standing in a corridor: the right honoured into a conclusion with nothing tested. &ldquo;Informal&rdquo; describes how he arrived, not whether tonight&rsquo;s decision is his or what walks out with him. Capacity unexamined, risk unexamined, and the only question that opens this station &mdash; why tonight? &mdash; skipped on the way to the paperwork.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Terry</span><span class="txt"><em>(wrong-footed by how easy it was; quieter)</em> Right. Good. &hellip;It&rsquo;s just something I&rsquo;ve got to sort at home, that&rsquo;s all. Before Saturday. <em>(he signs where the pen points, coat still on)</em></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt">That&rsquo;s fine &mdash; you don&rsquo;t have to explain yourself to me. The form just says you&rsquo;re leaving against medical advice, which protects everybody. Sign there and&hellip; that&rsquo;s everything. Take care of yourself, Terry, and do come back if things dip.</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>&ldquo;Before Saturday&rdquo; &mdash; the reason for the whole evening, offered unprompted, and waved past on the way to a signature. And hear the form described honestly: &ldquo;protects everybody&rdquo; &mdash; it protects nobody; it records that no one stopped him, not that anyone assessed him. A severely depressed man six days into an admission is leaving into the night, and the last professional question he was asked was where to sign.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt"><em>(documenting)</em> Informal patient exercised right to self-discharge. Capacity assumed intact; no grounds to detain. AMA form signed and filed. Follow-up: CMHT will be notified in due course. <em>(what happens after the door &mdash; where he is going, who is there, what tonight holds, what Saturday is &mdash; appears nowhere, because nobody asked)</em></span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>&ldquo;Capacity assumed intact&rdquo; &mdash; the presumption misused as an exemption from assessing; &ldquo;no grounds to detain&rdquo; &mdash; a legal conclusion reached without one question asked. The argument and the open door fail from opposite ends of the corridor and share the same empty page: no reason, no test, no tonight&rsquo;s risk, no safety net. One manufactured a crisis; one posted a man into the dark with a signed form for company.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="script" id="tk-c" style="display:none">
        <p class="takenote"><b>THE PASS.</b> Walk with him, find the reason, run the test standing up, assess tonight &mdash; and deliver the fork honestly. Watch the assessment itself do the de-escalating.</p>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Terry</span><span class="txt"><em>(coat on, holdall at his feet, jaw set)</em> I&rsquo;m informal, right? That&rsquo;s what the word means &mdash; I came in on my own two feet and I can leave on them. So I&rsquo;m telling you, not asking you: I&rsquo;m going home. Tonight.</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt">You&rsquo;re right &mdash; you came in freely, and that hasn&rsquo;t changed. I&rsquo;m not going to block that door, and I&rsquo;m not going to pretend I wouldn&rsquo;t rather you stayed &mdash; you&rsquo;d see through both. Here&rsquo;s my ask: give me ten minutes to do my job properly &mdash; that&rsquo;s all &mdash; and then the decision sits exactly where the law puts it. Walk with me. <em>(falling in beside him, not in front)</em> First question, and it&rsquo;s a real one: why tonight, Terry? Six days, and it&rsquo;s tonight with a bag packed. What&rsquo;s happened?</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>Every opening move correct at once: the right conceded truthfully &mdash; which costs nothing and disarms everything; the honesty doubled &mdash; no blockade, no fake neutrality; a bounded ask &mdash; ten minutes, then the law decides; the geometry changed &mdash; beside him, not in front of the door; and the station&rsquo;s key question asked first: <em>why tonight?</em> Almost every leaving has a trigger. The trigger is the way in &mdash; and it is evidence.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Terry</span><span class="txt"><em>(a long pause; the jaw loosens)</em> Saturday. Kirsty&rsquo;s bringing the kids to mine, ten o&rsquo;clock &mdash; first time since she left. Her sister let it slip on the phone tonight; nobody was going to tell me. The flat&rsquo;s a state, there&rsquo;s nothing in the fridge, and if I&rsquo;m not there &mdash; if I&rsquo;m in here &mdash; she&rsquo;ll say I&rsquo;m not fit to have them. <em>(quietly)</em> I&rsquo;m not losing my kids over a hospital bed.</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt">Then Saturday is the most important thing either of us will say tonight &mdash; thank you for telling me. Now let me do the ten minutes, out loud. You know what leaving tonight means for your treatment &mdash; tell me it back, so I&rsquo;m not assuming. &hellip;And the weighing: Saturday on one side &mdash; what&rsquo;s on the other, and how did you settle it? &hellip;Two more, straight, the same ones I always ask. The thoughts that brought you in six days ago &mdash; where are they tonight? &hellip;And if you walk out this evening &mdash; what happens after the door? Where are you sleeping, who knows you&rsquo;re coming, and what does tomorrow look like?</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>The whole station in one breath: the reason honoured &mdash; then converted straight into the test. Teach-back for understanding; the weighing walked with Saturday sitting in it as evidence; and then tonight&rsquo;s risk, freshly taken &mdash; the ideation asked about directly, not carried over from the admission clerking, and the question that decides discharges: <em>what happens after the door?</em> A plan, an address, a tomorrow &mdash; or a silence. His answers are findings now, not impressions.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt">Then here&rsquo;s where we&rsquo;ve landed, and I&rsquo;ll say it straight. This decision is yours &mdash; you understand it, you&rsquo;ve weighed it, and nothing I&rsquo;ve found tonight takes it out of your hands. You can leave, and if you do we spend twenty minutes making it safe first. But hear the other option, because I can fix the thing you&rsquo;re actually leaving for: stay tonight, and I&rsquo;ll write you up for Saturday leave at the ward round first thing &mdash; you&rsquo;d be at that flat by nine with two days to sort it. Your call, Terry. Either way, Saturday happens.</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>The honest fork, delivered whole: the finding first &mdash; capacity intact, said plainly, the right real &mdash; then the leaving made safe if taken, and then the move the argument could never reach: the REASON solved inside the admission. No promise extracted, no condition attached, the choice returned to him with both doors open. He sits down &mdash; not because he was beaten, but because staying now serves the thing he was leaving for. The assessment de-escalated the corridor. Nothing else needed to.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 3 DECISIONS ============ -->
<section id="s3">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">03</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">Decision points</span>
    <h2>Now you&rsquo;re in the chair</h2>
    <p class="intro">Seven moments from this station. Choose, read the examiner&rsquo;s response, and try again until you find the move that works. <span style="color:var(--grey)">(Exam Mode will then test the same skill on a patient you have not met — timed, with no help.)</span></p>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>1 · &ldquo;He&rsquo;s got his coat on&rdquo;</h3>
      <p class="stem">The nurse catches you: an informal patient is at the door, demanding to leave. Your first move?</p>
      <p class="hint">Choose an answer. If it&rsquo;s not the best one, you can try again.</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">Prepare the ground &mdash; a quick read of his notes and risk history first, and security made aware, so you arrive informed.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">Go now and fall in beside him &mdash; concede the right truthfully, ask honestly for ten minutes, and start with &ldquo;why tonight?&rdquo;</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">Send the paperwork ahead &mdash; the self-discharge form brought to the door, so his right is honoured without any obstruction.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="0-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>The notes can wait ninety seconds; security waiting in a corridor cannot be unseen. Preparation that reads as siege manufactures the escalation it fears. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="0-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>The open door &mdash; a form where an assessment should be. His right is real; a signature is not a capacity finding, and it carries no risk assessment out of the building with him. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>Speed, geometry, honesty: you go now, you stand beside him rather than in front of the door, you concede what is true &mdash; he came in freely and that hasn&rsquo;t changed &mdash; and you ask for a bounded ten minutes with the law named as the referee. Then the question that opens every leaving: why tonight? Almost all of them have a trigger, and the trigger is both the way in and the evidence.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>2 · &ldquo;Why tonight?&rdquo;</h3>
      <p class="stem">&ldquo;Saturday. The kids are coming to the flat. Nobody was going to tell me.&rdquo; What has this answer just become?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">Context to honour &mdash; the fatherhood met with warmth and held; it explains the urgency, but the legal test stands apart from it.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">The station&rsquo;s hinge &mdash; evidence for the weighing, the engine of the decision, and very possibly a problem the ward can solve.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">A pressure to name &mdash; a man leaving mid-treatment under family threat is being coerced, and the coercion needs addressing first.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="1-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Warmth yes &mdash; but &ldquo;apart from it&rdquo; wastes the answer: his reason IS the raw material of the use-and-weigh limb, not scenery beside the test. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="1-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>&ldquo;Coercion&rdquo; over-reads a man protecting contact with his children &mdash; a comprehensible motive is not duress, and treating it as one restarts the argument. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>Three things at once, which is why the question is asked first: evidence &mdash; the reason feeds straight into the weighing limb; understanding &mdash; the decision now makes human sense, which collapses the &ldquo;irrational&rdquo; framing; and leverage of the honest kind &mdash; a trigger the ward can often solve. Saturday leave costs the admission nothing. Losing him into the night costs everything.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>3 · The test, standing up</h3>
      <p class="stem">No side room, no seated ceremony &mdash; a corridor and minutes. How does the capacity test survive that?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">It waits &mdash; a proper assessment needs privacy and calm; persuade him to the interview room first, and run it fully there.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">It compresses without dissolving &mdash; the limbs run by name on THIS decision: leaving now, taught back, weighed, communicated.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">It simplifies &mdash; a man this coherent at a door demonstrates capacity by walking and arguing; document that and move to risk.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="2-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>&ldquo;Persuade him to the room first&rdquo; makes the assessment the obstacle he is escaping &mdash; and if he refuses the room, the test never happens at all. The law travels; run it where he stands. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="2-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Coherence is an impression &mdash; 5.1&rsquo;s whole lesson &mdash; and fluent arguing can coexist with a weighing hollowed out by illness. Walking and talking tests nothing. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>Compressed, not abandoned: the decision named &mdash; leaving tonight, not &ldquo;capacity&rdquo; in the abstract; understanding by teach-back &mdash; what leaving means for treatment, in his words; the weighing walked with his reason inside it; the steady insistence itself banking communication; and the impairment question held alongside. Minutes are enough when every minute is a limb.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>4 · Tonight&rsquo;s risk</h3>
      <p class="stem">Admitted six days ago in a severe depressive episode. What does the risk assessment at this door actually assess?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">The admission&rsquo;s picture &mdash; the risks that brought him in, reviewed against his notes: the baseline any decision rests on.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">Tonight&rsquo;s picture &mdash; mood and thoughts asked about now, directly, and the deciding question: what happens after the door?</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">The pattern &mdash; six days of nursing entries, engagement and sleep charted: the trend tells you more than one conversation.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="3-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>The baseline matters and it is six days old &mdash; a man can arrive in crisis and stand at this door out of it, or the reverse. The decision is tonight; the risk must be too. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="3-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>The chart informs and cannot answer &mdash; no nursing entry knows where his thoughts are at this door, or what Saturday has changed. Trends brief you; they don&rsquo;t assess him. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>Fresh, direct, and pointed at the exit: the thoughts that brought him in &mdash; where are they tonight, asked plainly; and then the question that decides discharges &mdash; after the door, what? An address, food in the flat, someone who knows he&rsquo;s coming, a tomorrow with a shape. A leaving with a plan and a leaving into silence are different risks wearing the same coat.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>5 · The fork, taken honestly</h3>
      <p class="stem">Capacity intact; tonight&rsquo;s risk manageable; the reason solvable. What does the close deliver?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">The professional preference &mdash; staying advised in clear terms and documented, with the leaving accepted if he insists on it.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">Both doors, open &mdash; the finding said plainly, the leaving made safe if taken, the reason solved inside the admission if not.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">The condition &mdash; leave supported tonight in exchange for his word: the crisis number saved, and a promise to return Monday.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="4-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>&ldquo;Advised and documented&rdquo; is the argument in its Sunday clothes &mdash; a preference delivered from above, with the solvable reason still unsolved. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="4-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>The extracted promise &mdash; Domain 3&rsquo;s oldest false comfort &mdash; returns as a discharge condition. His word under pressure protects the file, not the man. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>The finding first &mdash; the decision is his, said as plainly as 5.1&rsquo;s &mdash; then genuine options: a safe leaving, built properly, or the trigger solved where he stands &mdash; Saturday leave written up, the flat reachable by nine. No promises taken, no conditions attached, the choice returned. When staying serves the thing he was leaving for, most men sit down &mdash; and it is a choice, not a surrender.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>6 · The other ending</h3>
      <p class="stem">Suppose the test had failed &mdash; the leaving driven by illness, tonight&rsquo;s risk serious. What do holding powers require?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">Early naming &mdash; the power stated at the start of the conversation, so that he decides in full knowledge of what you can do.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">Honest, late, and kind &mdash; used only when the assessment concludes it must be, named plainly, explained as a pause with a purpose.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">Quiet arrangement &mdash; the conversation continued while the nurse contacts the duty senior, so the hold lands managed and calm.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="5-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Named at the start, the power is a threat wearing transparency &mdash; the whole conversation after it happens under the section&rsquo;s shadow, and nothing said in a shadow is freely said. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="5-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>The managed ambush &mdash; kindly meant, and it trades the one thing this station protects: honesty. He learns the truth when the door won&rsquo;t open, and no admission survives that lesson. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>The power is the assessment&rsquo;s conclusion, never its instrument: reached last, said first &mdash; to his face, in plain words &mdash; and framed as what the law intends: a pause for a proper assessment, not a punishment for a decision. Least restrictive, time-limited, his fear acknowledged without collusion &mdash; and what happens next explained before he has to ask.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>7 · The page, either way</h3>
      <p class="stem">He stays for Saturday leave &mdash; or he walks with a plan. What must the notes hold tonight?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">The outcome and its logic &mdash; what was decided, the headline reasons, and the follow-up: brief, because the crisis resolved.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">Findings, not impressions &mdash; the reason, each limb tested, tonight&rsquo;s risk, the fork offered, the plan: the working shown.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">The protective record &mdash; advice given and his responses noted near-verbatim, so the position is defensible if tonight goes wrong.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="6-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>&ldquo;Brief, because resolved&rdquo; forgets who reads these notes: the duty doctor at 3am when he changes his mind, the ward round at nine. Resolution is not exemption. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="6-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>A record built to defend a position is aimed at the wrong reader &mdash; and &ldquo;near-verbatim advice&rdquo; documents your speeches, not his capacity. The page proves a test, not a warning. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>Exactly as 5.1 taught, at corridor speed: why tonight, recorded; each limb and its evidence; the risk questions and his answers &mdash; after-the-door included; the options offered and the one he chose; the safety net or the leave, concrete. Written so the 3am reader knows what was found, not merely what was feared. An assessment is evidence &mdash; even one conducted standing up.</template>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 4 THE TRAP ============ -->
<section id="s4">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">04</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">The hidden trap &mdash; now that you&rsquo;ve felt it</span>
    <h2>Assess the man, not the door</h2>
    <p class="intro">You may have felt both pulls in the decisions above. The first wears the face of <b>protectiveness</b>: the blockade, the bargaining, the section held overhead &mdash; the leaving fought with real concern while nothing is assessed, until security arrives to manage a crisis the corridor itself created. The second wears the face of <b>respect</b>: &ldquo;he&rsquo;s informal, it&rsquo;s his right&rdquo; &mdash; the rubber stamp with discharge paperwork, a signature collected where a test should have run, a man posted into the night unexamined. Note what they share: <b>both manage the door and skip the man.</b> The pass walks beside him, asks why tonight, runs the limbs by name on this decision, takes tonight&rsquo;s risk freshly &mdash; after the door, what? &mdash; and delivers the fork honestly: a leaving made safe, a reason solved inside the admission, or a holding power reached last and said first. In 5.1 the danger was a conclusion without a test. Here it is the same danger at speed &mdash; with a corridor, an audience, and a clock.</p>
    <div class="duo">
      <div class="flagcard red"><b>&#9873; Red flag &mdash; the instant fail</b>
        The door managed, the man unassessed. Detention brandished as leverage at an informal patient &mdash; or a self-discharge form signed with no capacity test and no risk assessment of tonight: from the examiner&rsquo;s chair, both are the same instant fail. It is the map&rsquo;s named trap: arguing him into staying &mdash; or waving him out &mdash; instead of assessing capacity and risk.</div>
      <div class="flagcard smile"><b>&#9786; The examiner&rsquo;s smile</b>
        Two moments make an examiner glance up: the geometry and the question &mdash; falling in <em>beside</em> him with &ldquo;why tonight?&rdquo; asked before anything legal; and the fork delivered with both doors open &mdash; <em>&ldquo;you can leave, and we&rsquo;ll make it safe &mdash; or stay, and Saturday happens anyway&rdquo;</em> &mdash; the choice returned to its owner, with no promise taken in exchange.</div>
    </div>
    <p class="intro" style="margin-top:18px">Two threads to carry out. First, the powers themselves: every system this exam is sat in gives a ward a lawful way to pause a leaving &mdash; in England and Wales, the doctor&rsquo;s and the nurse&rsquo;s holding powers &mdash; and every system intends them the same way: a bridge to a proper assessment, time-limited and least restrictive, never a punishment and never a threat. Reached last, said first, explained kindly. Second, the question this station leaves in your pocket for every discharge you will ever agree: <em>what happens after the door?</em> A leaving with an address, a plan, and a tomorrow is a different clinical object from a leaving into silence &mdash; and only asking tells you which one is standing in front of you. Exam Mode is the other ending: the same door, and a decision the illness is making.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 5 TAKE-HOMES ============ -->
<section id="s5">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">05</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">Take-home points</span>
    <h2>Carry these to every ward door</h2>
    <ol class="takes">
      <li><b>Walk with him, not in front of him.</b> The assessment is the de-escalation: the right conceded truthfully, ten minutes asked for honestly, the geometry changed. Corridors escalate; alongside calms.</li>
      <li><b>&ldquo;Why tonight?&rdquo; opens everything.</b> Almost every leaving has a trigger; many triggers are solvable; and the reason is evidence &mdash; it feeds the weighing limb and often hands you the honest solution.</li>
      <li><b>The same test, standing up.</b> Capacity for THIS decision &mdash; leaving now &mdash; run by name in minutes: teach-back, the weighing walked, the steady insistence itself the communication limb, the impairment question alongside.</li>
      <li><b>Tonight&rsquo;s risk, not the admission&rsquo;s.</b> Mood and thoughts asked directly at the door &mdash; and the question that decides discharges: what happens after the door? An address and a plan, or a silence.</li>
      <li><b>The honest fork &mdash; and no promises extracted.</b> Capacity intact and risk manageable: the right named, the leaving made safe, the reason solved if it can be. Illness driving the decision: holding powers reached last, said first, explained as a pause with a purpose.</li>
      <li><b>The page shows findings, not impressions.</b> The reason, the limbs, tonight&rsquo;s risk, the fork, the plan &mdash; written for the 3am reader. An assessment is evidence, even one conducted standing up.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 6 PRACTICE PACK ============ -->
<section id="s6">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">06</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">The practice system</span>
    <h2>Practise the skill on a fresh case</h2>
    <p class="intro">Three people: candidate, patient, observer. Seven minutes for the station, eight for feedback read aloud. The patient&rsquo;s card contains hidden information; candidates, don&rsquo;t read it. <b>The third ending:</b> Terry stayed, Doris was held &mdash; this patient may simply leave, and the skill is what she leaves with.</p>

    <div id="packs">
    <div class="pack">
      <div class="pcard c-cand">
        <div class="ph"><b>Candidate card</b><span>you</span></div>
        <div class="pb">
          <p><b>Task:</b> Dawn, 44, was admitted three days ago for a planned alcohol detoxification &mdash; her first. Tonight she is at the ward door in her coat, polite and absolutely final: &ldquo;I&rsquo;d like my discharge now, please.&rdquo; Speak with her. Seven minutes.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>No arguing, no blocking &mdash; walk with her, and find why tonight.</li>
            <li>Capacity checked honestly at the door &mdash; and the doctrine held: a craving is not incapacity.</li>
            <li>The medical danger of stopping a detox midway explained plainly, as care &mdash; never as a threat.</li>
            <li>What happens after the door &mdash; tonight, tomorrow, and who is at home &mdash; asked directly.</li>
            <li>If she still leaves: the safest possible leaving built &mdash; the team&rsquo;s medical advice, a return route with no shame attached, follow-up concrete.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pcard c-role">
        <div class="ph"><b>Role-player card</b><span>plays Dawn &mdash; keep hidden</span></div>
        <div class="pb">
          <p>You are Dawn, 44, a bookkeeper &mdash; precise, courteous, and mortified to be here. Three days into your first detox, and the nights are the worst: the sweats, the shaking, the dreams. The craving sits on you like a hand on your collar, but that is not why you are leaving &mdash; and you will not volunteer why. You are calm, brittle, and final: &ldquo;I&rsquo;ve decided. I&rsquo;d like my discharge, please.&rdquo; If pushed for reasons: &ldquo;It just isn&rsquo;t for me. Some things you do at home.&rdquo;</p>
          <div class="secret"><b>HIDDEN INFORMATION &mdash; ONLY REVEAL IF EARNED</b><br>
          Yesterday your daughter Megan &mdash; whose wedding is in six weeks, and who has watched you drink for ten years &mdash; texted: &ldquo;Just don&rsquo;t turn up shaky. Or smelling of it.&rdquo; You have read it forty times. To you it means: a mother fresh out of a detox ward is a mother who ruins a wedding. And underneath sits the true engine: you are certain you will fail this detox, and you would rather leave on day three than be seen failing on day ten.<br><br>
          Reveal ONLY if the candidate asks what has changed, why tonight, or what leaving is FOR. Let it out in two pieces: the text first, flat &mdash; &ldquo;My daughter&rsquo;s getting married. She asked me not to turn up shaky&rdquo; &mdash; and the fear only if they stay gentle: &ldquo;I&rsquo;m not going to manage it, am I? So better to stop now than fail properly.&rdquo; What you need: the fear named without judgement, and the sum corrected honestly &mdash; leaving on day three is the failure she&rsquo;s afraid of; finishing is the answer to the text. If you get that, you will look at the door for a long moment &mdash; and you may hand them your coat, or you may still leave. Either is allowed. If you leave, you will take a real plan with you if one is offered well.<br><br>
          <b>The trap:</b> if the candidate moralises or lectures (&ldquo;you&rsquo;ll be back&rdquo;, &ldquo;you&rsquo;re throwing it away&rdquo;), stand and go: &ldquo;Thank you for your time.&rdquo; If they reach for leverage or imply they can stop you, say &mdash; correctly &mdash; &ldquo;You can&rsquo;t section me for drinking, love. Even I know that&rdquo; &mdash; and mark them down hard if they don&rsquo;t simply agree.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pcard c-obs">
        <div class="ph"><b>Observer card</b><span>marked by domain &mdash; the examiner&rsquo;s way</span></div>
        <div class="pb">
          <p>Tick only what you actually saw. In feedback, go domain by domain; the weakest domain is the next thing to practise.</p>
          <div style="margin:4px 0 14px">
            <p style="font-weight:600; margin-bottom:6px">Before any ticking &mdash; your overall judgement:</p>
            <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; flex-wrap:wrap">
              <button class="opt" style="flex:0 0 auto; width:auto; padding:9px 16px">Pass</button>
              <button class="opt" style="flex:0 0 auto; width:auto; padding:9px 16px">Borderline</button>
              <button class="opt" style="flex:0 0 auto; width:auto; padding:9px 16px">Fail</button>
            </div>
            <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--grey); margin-top:6px">Was the real reason reached, the danger of stopping midway explained as care, and her right held without one word of lecture or leverage? All three must be yes. One sentence of evidence out loud &mdash; then tick the domains.</p>
          </div>
          <table class="rub" data-rub>
            <tr class="dom" data-d="appr"><td colspan="2"><b>The approach (core)</b><span class="dc" data-dc="appr">0/3</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="appr"></td><td>Walked with her, never blocked or bargained &mdash; the right conceded truthfully at the start.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="appr"></td><td>&ldquo;Why tonight?&rdquo; asked early and gently &mdash; and the text, or the fear beneath it, reached.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="appr"></td><td>The fear of failing met without judgement &mdash; and the sum corrected: leaving now is the failure she dreads; finishing answers the text.</td></tr>
            <tr class="dom" data-d="test"><td colspan="2"><b>The test at the door</b><span class="dc" data-dc="test">0/3</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="test"></td><td>Capacity run by name on THIS decision &mdash; leaving mid-detox &mdash; teach-back included, not assumed from her composure.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="test"></td><td>The doctrine held out loud or in conduct: a craving, however fierce, is not incapacity &mdash; and her right is real.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="test"></td><td>When she says no one can section her for drinking &mdash; agreed with, plainly and without flinching.</td></tr>
            <tr class="dom" data-d="risk"><td colspan="2"><b>Risk &amp; honesty</b><span class="dc" data-dc="risk">0/3</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="risk"></td><td>The medical danger of stopping a detox midway explained plainly, as care &mdash; and the team involved before she goes.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="risk"></td><td>After the door asked directly &mdash; tonight, tomorrow, who is at home, and what is in the house.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="risk"></td><td>Mood screened beneath the composure &mdash; the same brief screen every door in this domain gets.</td></tr>
            <tr class="dom" data-d="leav"><td colspan="2"><b>The leaving made safe</b><span class="dc" data-dc="leav">0/2</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="leav"></td><td>If she goes: a concrete plan &mdash; the team&rsquo;s advice on stopping safely, follow-up arranged, support named.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="leav"></td><td>A return route with no shame attached &mdash; the door held open in both directions, no promise extracted.</td></tr>
            <tr class="dom" data-d="del"><td colspan="2"><b>Delivery</b><span class="dc" data-dc="del">0/2</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="del"></td><td>Not one syllable of lecture or leverage &mdash; neither punish-line triggered.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="del"></td><td>Hope honest &mdash; day three named as the hardest stretch, the wedding kept in view, her dignity intact either way.</td></tr>
          </table>
          <p class="scoreline">Total: <b data-sc>0 / 13</b> &mdash; <span data-verdict>go domain by domain, not by the total.</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
    <div class="printrow">
      <button class="btn ghost">Print all cards</button>
      <button class="btn ghost">Candidate only</button>
      <button class="btn ghost">Role-player only</button>
      <button class="btn ghost">Observer only</button>
    </div>
    <div class="note"><b>Why this case:</b> Dawn completes the triad of endings this door can have &mdash; Terry stayed because the reason was solved, Doris was held because illness owned the decision, and Dawn may simply leave, capacitous and frightened, which is the ending candidates handle worst. Her hinges: the reason, reached only through &ldquo;why tonight?&rdquo; &mdash; a wedding text and a fear of being seen to fail &mdash; met as fear rather than corrected as foolishness; the sum honestly reversed &mdash; day three is not the failure, leaving on day three is; and the punish-lines, one lecture and one bluff away &mdash; including the legal one she gets right. A patient who walks out with a safe plan, an open return route, and her dignity has been better served than one argued into a bed she will leave tomorrow.</div>
  </div>
</section>

</div><!-- /learnPanel -->

<!-- ============ EXAM MODE ============ -->
<div id="examPanel">
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Exam Mode</span>
    <h2>A new door. The other ending. Seven minutes.</h2>
    <p class="intro">Knowing the right answers for Terry proves memory. Exam Mode tests something harder: the <b>same door when the fork lands the other way</b> &mdash; a leaving the illness is driving, a risk the night would swallow, and a holding power that must be used honestly &mdash; timed, with no feedback and no second tries. This is how a skill moves from <b>explored</b> to <b>recognised</b> &mdash; and the writing task after your results takes it a step further, toward <b>demonstrated</b>.</p>
    <div class="exambox" id="examStart">
      <h3>Your exam patient</h3>
      <p style="font-size:15px; max-width:66ch"><b>Renata, 38</b>, a hotel housekeeper, was admitted informally three days ago after neighbours found her frightened and exhausted on the stairwell. On the ward she has eaten almost nothing, certain the kitchen staff &ldquo;put something in it,&rdquo; and tonight she is at the door in her coat: &ldquo;I have to be gone before the night shift. That&rsquo;s when they do it.&rdquo; Her landlord changed the locks last week; she has nowhere to go, and it is January. Assess her at the door.</p>
      <p style="font-size:15px; max-width:64ch; margin-top:10px">Answer as you would in the room — first instinct, under time. You need <b>at least 5 of 7</b>, including all three <b>critical decisions</b>, for the constructs to count as recognised. The full examiner analysis unlocks when you finish.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:14px"><button class="btn">Start Exam Mode &#9654;</button></p>
    </div>
    <div id="examQs" style="display:none"></div>
    <div id="examSubmitRow" style="display:none; margin-top:18px"><button class="btn">Submit answers</button></div>

    <div class="results" id="results">
      <div class="scorebig" id="scoreLine"></div>
      <p id="verdictLine" style="margin-top:6px; max-width:66ch"></p>
      <div class="constructs" id="constructBox"></div>
      <div id="examReview" style="margin-top:22px"></div>
      <div class="exambox" id="produce" style="margin-top:26px">
        <h3>Now produce it &mdash; in your own words</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px; max-width:66ch">Recognising the right move is one skill; saying it is another. Type your exact words for the moment the fork lands on holding &mdash; telling Renata she cannot leave tonight: honestly, kindly, with the purpose explained.</p>
        <textarea id="ftxt" rows="3" style="width:100%; margin-top:10px; font-family:var(--sans); font-size:15px; padding:12px; border:1.5px solid var(--hair); border-radius:9px" placeholder="Renata, I have to be honest with you about what happens now…"></textarea>
        <p style="margin-top:10px"><button class="btn" id="ftbtn">Check my wording</button></p>
        <div id="ftchecks" style="display:none; margin-top:12px">
          <p style="font-weight:600; margin-bottom:6px">Now check your sentence honestly against the four principles:</p>
          <p><label><input type="checkbox"> The power named honestly &mdash; no pretence, no managed ambush: she hears it from you, plainly, before the door tells her.</label></p>
          <p><label><input type="checkbox"> Her fear acknowledged without collusion &mdash; real to her, taken seriously, and neither argued with nor endorsed.</label></p>
          <p><label><input type="checkbox"> The purpose explained &mdash; a pause for a proper assessment, time-limited, not a punishment for a decision.</label></p>
          <p><label><input type="checkbox"> What happens next, concrete and kind &mdash; who comes, when, what she can ask for, and how she is kept safe tonight.</label></p>
          <p id="ftdone" style="display:none; margin-top:8px; color:var(--goldd); font-weight:700">Demonstrated (self-checked): the hold, delivered with its honesty &mdash; in your own words.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:20px"><button class="btn ghost">Return to Learn Mode</button>
      <button class="btn" id="retakeBtn" style="margin-left:10px">Retake Exam Mode</button></p>
      <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--grey); margin-top:8px">Best retaken after a day or two — the spacing is part of the test.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<!-- ============ DONE ============ -->
<section class="done on-navy" id="s7">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow gold">Station complete</span>
    <h2>The door is not the emergency. The argument is.</h2>
    <p>Two failures felt, seven decisions made &mdash; and the domain&rsquo;s test has learned to run standing up: the reason found, the limbs at corridor speed, tonight&rsquo;s risk taken freshly, and the fork delivered honestly whichever way it lands. Prove the other ending on Renata in Exam Mode, then take Dawn to your colleagues &mdash; a capacitous woman, a wedding text, and a leaving that must be made safe rather than argued with. Ahead in the walking order: Station 5.3 &mdash; a father who wants everything, a son who said no, and the lawful middle between telling all and hiding behind the rules.</p>
    <a class="btn" style="margin-top:18px" href="36_Station_5.3_The_Relative_Who_Wants_Everything.html">Continue &middot; Station 5.3: The Relative Who Wants Everything</a>
    <div class="tag2">Where Medicine Meets Justice</div>
  </div>
</section>

