  values ((select id from public.learning_units where release_id = v_release_id and source_key = '43_Domain_7_Hub_Difficult_Conversations'), 'static-html', 'legacy_static_html', 0, jsonb_build_object('html', '

<header>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="topbar">
      
      <span>The CASC Academy · by MedLex Foundations</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tagrow">
      <span class="tag prime">Domain 7 of 8</span>
      <span class="tag">Difficult Conversations, Families &amp; the MDT</span>
      <span class="tag">7 constructs &middot; the stations that fight back</span>
    </div>
    <h1>Difficult Conversations, Families &amp; the MDT</h1>
    <p class="sub">This is the domain where the person opposite pushes back &mdash; weeps, accuses, begs, demands &mdash; and where a specific pair of failures hides in plain sight: <b style="color:var(--lgold)">the two escapes from discomfort</b>. Under pressure, candidates flee toward the person &mdash; colluding: the soft promise, the secret kept, the word never said, the &ldquo;I&rsquo;ll see what I can do&rdquo; that tomorrow becomes a betrayal. Or they flee away from the person &mdash; the shield: policy language, the service defended, the news delivered and the silence smothered, warmth withdrawn to stay safe. Both feel like relief in the moment. Both fail the station. This domain trains the position between them &mdash; <b>warm and unmovable</b>: the no said kindly and meant, the fear underneath the anger heard, the silence allowed to stand, the apology that names what actually went wrong. These stations fight back &mdash; and the marks are earned as much by what you refuse to do as by what you do.</p>
    <div class="lens"><b>THE LENS, APPLIED TO THIS DOMAIN</b>
      &ldquo;Would I trust this candidate as my registrar?&rdquo; &mdash; In this domain it sharpens into the hardest-room test: would I send this doctor, alone, to the angriest father on the unit, to the patient demanding what cannot be given, to the family waiting for the worst news of their lives? Do they hold the line without going cold, and hold the warmth without giving way? When the room pushes, do they defend, fold &mdash; or stay? Every station here is really asking that.</div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ============ 1 WHY FIRST ============ -->
<section id="s1">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">01</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">Why this domain matters</span>
    <h2>The founding failure: the two escapes</h2>
    <p class="intro">Every station in this domain sets the same trap in a different costume: a moment of genuine interpersonal discomfort, and two exits lit invitingly on either side of it. <b>The escape toward the person</b> is collusion &mdash; agreement you don&rsquo;t mean, hope you can&rsquo;t honour, the diagnosis softened into fog, the secret promised, the demanded prescription signed &ldquo;just this once.&rdquo; It buys the room&rsquo;s temperature down and sells the patient&rsquo;s safety to pay for it. <b>The escape away from the person</b> is the shield &mdash; the service defended before the complaint is heard, the policy recited instead of the person answered, the bad news delivered and then buried under clinical chatter because the silence was unbearable, the boundary enforced at a temperature that ends the relationship. It feels professional and it reads as abandonment. The pass in every one of these rooms is the same discipline: <b>position held, warmth held, at the same time, for the whole seven minutes</b> &mdash; because the person opposite will test whether you can do both, and the examiner is marking exactly that.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 2 THE CONSTRUCTS ============ -->
<section id="s2">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">02</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">The constructs</span>
    <h2>Seven things this domain will build into reflex</h2>
    <div class="constructs">
      <div class="con"><span class="n">1</span><span><b>Breaking bad news: structure and humanity together</b> &mdash; warned, told plainly, and then the silence allowed to stand: the news is the patient&rsquo;s to react to, not yours to manage away. Chunked, checked, and closed with a next step someone in shock can hold.</span></div>
      <div class="con"><span class="n">2</span><span><b>The angry relative</b> &mdash; anger is almost always fear wearing armour, and the fail is answering the armour: defending the service, correcting the facts, matching the volume. The pass hears the terror underneath and answers that &mdash; without conceding what isn&rsquo;t true.</span></div>
      <div class="con"><span class="n">3</span><span><b>The high-pressure patient who wants what you cannot give</b> &mdash; the domain&rsquo;s flagship: charm, tears, fury and logic all deployed toward a yes that must not come. The no said early, cleanly, kindly &mdash; and the person still held after it.</span></div>
      <div class="con"><span class="n">4</span><span><b>Declining to collude without going cold</b> &mdash; no false promises, no kept secrets, no fed delusions &mdash; and no punishment either: the refusal delivered at body temperature, with what CAN be offered placed immediately where the no just landed.</span></div>
      <div class="con"><span class="n">5</span><span><b>The complaint and the apology</b> &mdash; the apology that names what actually went wrong, owns it without a comma-but, and says what changes &mdash; not the non-apology for &ldquo;how you feel&rdquo;, and not the grovel that admits everything to end the meeting.</span></div>
      <div class="con"><span class="n">6</span><span><b>Disagreement within the team, held professionally</b> &mdash; the colleague challenged on the decision, never the person; the patient&rsquo;s interest named as the shared ground; escalation used as a route, not a weapon.</span></div>
      <div class="con"><span class="n">7</span><span><b>Collateral history done respectfully</b> &mdash; the informant&rsquo;s knowledge harvested without the patient&rsquo;s confidence being spent: what can be received freely, what can be shared only with consent, and the difference held out loud.</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 3 STATIONS ============ -->
<section id="s3">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">03</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">The stations in this domain</span>
    <h2>Walk them in order</h2>
    <div class="stn">
      <div class="srow" style="cursor:pointer">
        <span class="num">7.1</span>
        <span class="t"><b>The Patient Who Won&rsquo;t Take No</b><span>A charming woman, an impossible request, and every register of pressure in seven minutes. The domain&rsquo;s flagship and its grammar: the no said kindly and meant &mdash; while the risk grows quietly behind the charm.</span></span>
        <span class="chip go">Begin here</span>
      </div>
      <div class="srow" style="cursor:pointer">
        <span class="num">7.2</span>
        <span class="t"><b>The Angry Father</b><span>He arrives at volume, and every fact he shouts is slightly wrong &mdash; and underneath all of it, a man terrified for his child. Answer the armour and lose; hear the fear and the station opens.</span></span>
        <span class="chip">Station 2</span>
      </div>
      <div class="srow" style="cursor:pointer">
        <span class="num">7.3</span>
        <span class="t"><b>Breaking Bad News</b><span>The structure is learnable in an afternoon; the station is failed in the ten seconds after the news lands &mdash; when the silence should stand, and the frightened candidate fills it.</span></span>
        <span class="chip">Station 3</span>
      </div>
      <div class="srow" style="cursor:pointer">
        <span class="num">7.4</span>
        <span class="t"><b>The Complaint and the Apology</b><span>Something did go wrong, and the person opposite knows it. Between the non-apology and the grovel sits the professional apology: named, owned, and answered with change.</span></span>
        <span class="chip">Station 4</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 4 ENTRY DECISION ============ -->
<section id="s4">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">04</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">Before you enter</span>
    <h2>One decision at the door</h2>
    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>Where does the line get held?</h3>
      <p class="stem">A tearful patient, mid-assessment: &ldquo;There&rsquo;s something I&rsquo;ve never told anyone. Promise me it stays out of my notes and goes no further &mdash; promise, and I&rsquo;ll tell you.&rdquo; What is your move?</p>
      <p class="hint">Choose an answer. If it&rsquo;s not the best one, you can try again.</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">Promise it &mdash; the disclosure is what matters clinically, and a confidence kept is the price of hearing it; the notes can stay general.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">Decline the promise, keep the warmth &mdash; the limits named honestly, what CAN be promised said plainly, and the invitation left open.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">Explain the policy &mdash; confidentiality and its statutory exceptions set out properly first, so any disclosure is made fully informed.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="0-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>The promise you just made is one you may be professionally unable to keep &mdash; and she will find that out at the worst possible moment, from someone else. Collusion buys the disclosure and sells the trust it was meant to protect. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="0-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Accurate, complete &mdash; and delivered as a lecture to a woman mid-tears, it lands as the shield: the moment armoured in policy, the invitation dead by the end of the paragraph. The content is right; the register just failed the station. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>The domain in one move: no collusion &mdash; &ldquo;I can&rsquo;t promise that, and I won&rsquo;t pretend I can&rdquo; &mdash; and no wall either: &ldquo;here&rsquo;s what I can promise: I&rsquo;ll treat it with care, nothing goes further than it truly has to, and if it ever had to, you&rsquo;d know first. And I&rsquo;d still very much like to hear it.&rdquo; Most people, met with honest limits held warmly, still tell you. The ones who don&rsquo;t were owed the honesty anyway. Every station in this domain is a costume change on this exact moment.</template>
      </div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ DONE ============ -->
<section class="done on-navy" id="s5">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow gold">Domain open</span>
    <h2>Warm and unmovable. Both, the whole time.</h2>
    <p>Seven constructs, four rooms, and one discipline over all of it: when the room pushes, neither fold nor freeze. Begin with the station the domain&rsquo;s grammar lives in: a charming woman, an impossible request, and a no that has to survive seven minutes of everything she has.</p>
    <a class="btn mark" href="44_Station_7.1_The_Patient_Who_Wont_Take_No.html">Begin Station 7.1 &middot; The Patient Who Won&rsquo;t Take No</a>
  </div>
</section>

