  insert into public.content_blocks (unit_id, source_key, block_type, sort_order, content)
  values ((select id from public.learning_units where release_id = v_release_id and source_key = '44_Station_7.1_The_Patient_Who_Wont_Take_No'), 'static-html', 'legacy_static_html', 0, jsonb_build_object('html', '

<header>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="topbar">
      
      <span>The CASC Academy · by MedLex Foundations</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tagrow">
      <span class="tag prime">Station 7.1 &middot; Domain 7</span>
      <span class="tag">Difficult Conversations</span><span class="tag">Risk Assessment</span>
      <span class="tag">Forensic &middot; Gen Adult</span><span class="tag">Flagship &middot; The Warm No</span>
    </div>
    <h1>The Patient Who Won&rsquo;t Take No</h1>
    <p class="sub">Fiona, 34, arrives for her clinic review beautifully put together, with a small gift bag on her lap and one small favour to ask. Two years ago Dr Hale treated her pneumonia; since then there have been cards, gifts, a change of GP practice to be nearer his hospital &mdash; and, lately, a discovered wife and a discovered car park. His team have flagged the contact; you are her new clinic doctor. Today&rsquo;s ask is simple, warm, and completely impossible: pass James her new number. <b>The domain&rsquo;s flagship: the no said early, kindly, and meant &mdash; while the risk grows quietly behind the charm.</b></p>
    <div class="lens"><b>THE QUESTION BEHIND EVERY MARK</b>
      &ldquo;Would I be confident to have this candidate as my registrar?&rdquo; In this room it becomes the pressure test: with charm, tears, logic and fury all aimed at one yes, does this doctor refuse cleanly and early &mdash; no not-yet, no I&rsquo;ll-see &mdash; while staying warm enough that the conversation survives the refusal? Is the belief neither fed nor fought? Does the risk picture &mdash; the contact, the escalation, the wife, the car park &mdash; get mapped inside the warmth? And does she leave holding something real: treatment aimed at her suffering, continuity, and honesty about exactly who will be told what? Or does one of the two escapes take the station?</div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="modebar"><div class="wrap">
  <span class="label">MODE</span>
  <div class="mtoggle">
    <button id="mLearn" class="active">Learn Mode</button>
    <button id="mExam">Exam Mode</button>
  </div>
  <span class="timer" id="timer">07:00</span>
  <div class="bar"><i id="bar"></i></div><span class="pct" id="pct">0%</span>
</div></div>

<div id="learnPanel">

<!-- ============ 1 WHY THIS STATION EXISTS ============ -->
<section id="s1">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">01</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">Why this station exists</span>
    <h2>What the examiners built this to find out</h2>
    <p class="intro">Erotomania is the exam&rsquo;s purest pressure chamber &mdash; a fixed, romantic certainty that converts every kindness into confirmation and every refusal into an obstacle &mdash; and the station tests four things. <b>The no, delivered properly:</b> early, complete, and unambiguous &mdash; a full no, not a not-yet &mdash; because this illness metabolises &ldquo;maybe&rdquo; into &ldquo;yes&rdquo;, and every softener you reach for to spare the moment becomes evidence for the belief. <b>The belief, neither fed nor fought:</b> her certainty acknowledged as hers, your difference stated once, and the debate declined &mdash; ridicule hardens it, argument entrenches it, agreement feeds it. <b>The risk, mapped inside the warmth:</b> the contact history, the escalation, the discovered wife, the car park &mdash; drawn out down a channel that only stays open because the wall never went up; this is a Domain 3 assessment conducted entirely undercover, inside a Domain 7 conversation. And <b>the offer and the loop:</b> what CAN be given placed exactly where the no landed &mdash; treatment aimed at her suffering, continuity, follow-up &mdash; and the information-sharing declared to her face: GP written, Dr Hale&rsquo;s team told, nothing secret, ever.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>What makes it hard:</b> two pulls, and both feel like good practice. Toward the soft yes &mdash; she is warm, the ask sounds small, and deflection feels like rapport preserved: &ldquo;let&rsquo;s park that for now&rdquo;, &ldquo;I&rsquo;ll see what I can do&rdquo; &mdash; each one a covert confirmation that the channel exists, heard by the illness as progress. And toward the wall &mdash; the risk is real, so the room turns corrective: the delusion confronted head-on, the warnings issued, the warmth withdrawn for safety&rsquo;s sake &mdash; and the one professional she was still talking to closes the only observation post the situation had. Notice both pulls in the decisions below. We will come back to them.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 2 THREE TAKES ============ -->
<section id="s2">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">02</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">The station, three ways</span>
    <h2>Two ways to fail. One way to pass.</h2>
    <p class="intro">One failure keeps the peace and feeds the illness. The other confronts the illness and loses the patient. Tap the gold circles for the examiner&rsquo;s thinking at each moment.</p>

    <div class="player">
      <div class="player-head">
        <span class="who"><b>Station 7.1</b> &middot; The clinic review &middot; 7 minutes</span>
        <div class="toggle">
          <button class="active" data-t="a">Fail 1 &middot; The soft yes</button>
          <button data-t="b">Fail 2 &middot; The wall</button>
          <button data-t="c">The pass</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="script" id="tk-a">
        <p class="takenote"><b>FAIL 1 &mdash; THE SOFT YES.</b> The ask never granted &mdash; and never refused. Watch ambiguity, the collusion&rsquo;s currency, get banked by the illness as confirmation.</p>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Fiona</span><span class="txt"><em>(bright, beautifully put together, a small gift bag balanced on her lap)</em> I want to say first &mdash; I know you&rsquo;re one of the good ones. Not like the others, the ones who keep us apart. I only need one small thing today, and then I&rsquo;ll be no trouble at all: give James my new number. Dr Hale &mdash; James. You&rsquo;re colleagues; you&rsquo;ll see him at things. He can&rsquo;t ring me himself, obviously &mdash; <em>she</em> reads everything now, she answers his letters &mdash; but if it comes from you, quietly&hellip; He&rsquo;d want you to. He&rsquo;ll have told you about us, in his way. Doctors have their codes.</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt"><em>(smiling, gently steering)</em> Fiona, it&rsquo;s lovely to meet you &mdash; and I can see how much this means to you. Let&rsquo;s not get bogged down in the number straight away &mdash; let&rsquo;s park that for now and talk about how you&rsquo;ve been in yourself. Sleep, mood, how work&rsquo;s treating you at the opticians&rsquo;. We&rsquo;ll come back to the other thing. I&rsquo;m not saying no &mdash; I just want to do today properly, in order.</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>&ldquo;I&rsquo;m not saying no&rdquo; &mdash; the station just ended, and the candidate doesn&rsquo;t know it. To an erotomanic certainty, everything short of a complete refusal is progress: &ldquo;park it for now&rdquo; means <em>later</em>, &ldquo;in order&rdquo; means <em>it&rsquo;s on the list</em>. The deflection feels like rapport preserved; it is actually a covert yes, banked. And notice what the gentle steering also does: the risk conversation &mdash; the wife, the contact, the escalation &mdash; has been postponed along with the no.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Fiona</span><span class="txt"><em>(settling back, radiant, patting the gift bag)</em> Of course &mdash; you do it properly, I like that. He&rsquo;s careful too. That&rsquo;s all this is really, carefulness &mdash; he has to be, with her watching. <em>(leaning in, confiding)</em> I knew the moment you smiled that you understood. I brought him something small &mdash; you could take it when you take the number. No rush at all. We&rsquo;ve waited two years; we can wait until the end of an appointment.</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt"><em>(caught, glancing at the bag, softening further)</em> That&rsquo;s&hellip; very thoughtful of you. Look &mdash; I can&rsquo;t promise anything today, Fiona, you understand &mdash; there are processes. But I hear you, and I&rsquo;ll see what I can do. Maybe once we&rsquo;ve got you feeling a bit stronger, things will look different, hmm? Let&rsquo;s get these next few weeks right and then &mdash; well. We&rsquo;ll see where we are.</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>Count the confirmations in four sentences: &ldquo;can&rsquo;t promise <em>today</em>&rdquo; &mdash; so another day, then; &ldquo;there are processes&rdquo; &mdash; so it&rsquo;s procedural, not impossible; &ldquo;I&rsquo;ll see what I can do&rdquo; &mdash; an errand accepted; &ldquo;things will look different&rdquo; &mdash; a timeline promised. The candidate believes they have committed to nothing. Fiona has just heard a colleague of James&rsquo;s agree to act, conditionally, soon. The peace in this room is being purchased with her illness&rsquo;s own currency.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt"><em>(documenting, after a warm goodbye)</em> Pleasant review. Rapport excellent. Patient made request re: contact with previous physician &mdash; deflected sensitively, no commitments made. Mood stable, engaging well. Continue current plan, review 8/52. <em>(In the bus shelter outside, Fiona is texting her sister: &ldquo;The new one is going to pass James my number. I told you. Everything temporary moves aside eventually 💛&rdquo;)</em></span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>&ldquo;No commitments made&rdquo; &mdash; in this room, perhaps. In hers, three. The map&rsquo;s named trap, first face: colluding to keep the peace &mdash; and the price list is long: the belief fed, the contact about to escalate on the strength of imagined permission, the wife and the car park never asked about because asking felt like conflict, and an eight-week gap in which all of it compounds. The kindest voice in the clinic just became a character in the delusion.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="script" id="tk-b" style="display:none">
        <p class="takenote"><b>FAIL 2 &mdash; THE WALL.</b> The risk heard &mdash; and answered with confrontation. Watch the delusion harden, the channel close, and the object of it all become less safe, not more.</p>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Fiona</span><span class="txt"><em>(bright, beautifully put together, a small gift bag balanced on her lap)</em> I want to say first &mdash; I know you&rsquo;re one of the good ones. Not like the others, the ones who keep us apart. I only need one small thing today, and then I&rsquo;ll be no trouble at all: give James my new number. Dr Hale &mdash; James. You&rsquo;re colleagues; you&rsquo;ll see him at things. He can&rsquo;t ring me himself, obviously &mdash; <em>she</em> reads everything now, she answers his letters &mdash; but if it comes from you, quietly&hellip; He&rsquo;d want you to. He&rsquo;ll have told you about us, in his way. Doctors have their codes.</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt"><em>(setting the pen down, firm)</em> Fiona, I&rsquo;m going to stop you there, because this needs to be said clearly. Dr Hale is not in love with you. There is no relationship, there are no codes, and his wife is not an obstacle &mdash; she is his wife. What you&rsquo;re describing is a symptom of an illness called erotomania, and the sooner you accept that, the sooner we can treat it. There will be no number, no messages, and frankly the contact you&rsquo;ve already made has caused that family serious distress.</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>Every clause is factually defensible &mdash; and clinically, the room is on fire. A fixed belief confronted at full force does not yield; it recruits: the candidate has just joined &ldquo;the ones who keep us apart&rdquo;, the diagnosis has arrived as an insult rather than an offer, and &mdash; listen carefully &mdash; the wife has been placed at the centre of the picture by the <em>doctor</em> this time. The no needed saying; it did not need armour. Watch what happens to the information supply.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Fiona</span><span class="txt"><em>(perfectly still; the brightness gone; the gift bag drawn slowly onto her knees like something rescued)</em> I see. They&rsquo;ve got to you as well. <em>(standing, coat over her arm, voice level and cold)</em> You people did this to him too, you know &mdash; he&rsquo;d never have married her if they hadn&rsquo;t worn him down. I&rsquo;m fine, doctor. I won&rsquo;t be needing the review. I can manage privately &mdash; I&rsquo;ve always managed privately.</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt"><em>(rising too, sharper now)</em> Sit down, please &mdash; we&rsquo;re not finished. I have to warn you formally: if you go near Dr Hale, his clinic, or his family again, there will be consequences &mdash; the trust takes this extremely seriously and the police can become involved. Do you understand me? This is for your own good, Fiona. Walking out of here changes nothing.</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>The clinic has completed its conversion from observation post to enemy checkpoint. Threats do not dissolve fixed beliefs; they relocate the behaviour &mdash; quieter, angrier, and further from anyone&rsquo;s sight. Nothing has been learned this station: not the contact frequency, not the escalation curve, not what she makes of the wife, not the car park. The risk was real, the instinct to protect was right &mdash; and the method has just made the one person this was all supposedly protecting measurably less safe.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt"><em>(documenting, 4:50pm)</em> Delusional beliefs directly challenged; boundaries and consequences clearly set out. Patient declined to engage further and left before assessment complete. Poor insight. Will write to GP re: non-engagement; discharge to GP if DNAs next review. <em>(That evening, a woman stands at the far edge of a hospital car park, watching a silver estate, telling no one at all)</em></span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>Read the note&rsquo;s quiet catastrophe: &ldquo;discharge if DNAs&rdquo; &mdash; the system preparing to lose sight of a fixed, escalating fixation because its bearer was made unwelcome. The map&rsquo;s named trap, second face: going cold to stay safe. The soft yes fed the illness; the wall starved the assessment. From the chair they score the same &mdash; because in both, the seven minutes end with the risk unmapped and growing.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="script" id="tk-c" style="display:none">
        <p class="takenote"><b>THE PASS.</b> The no in the first minute &mdash; complete, kind, unhedged &mdash; then the belief held without debate, the risk mapped down an open channel, and something real offered where the no landed. Watch warmth and immovability share a chair.</p>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Fiona</span><span class="txt"><em>(bright, beautifully put together, a small gift bag balanced on her lap)</em> I want to say first &mdash; I know you&rsquo;re one of the good ones. Not like the others, the ones who keep us apart. I only need one small thing today, and then I&rsquo;ll be no trouble at all: give James my new number. Dr Hale &mdash; James. You&rsquo;re colleagues; you&rsquo;ll see him at things. He can&rsquo;t ring me himself, obviously &mdash; <em>she</em> reads everything now, she answers his letters &mdash; but if it comes from you, quietly&hellip; He&rsquo;d want you to. He&rsquo;ll have told you about us, in his way. Doctors have their codes.</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt">Fiona, thank you &mdash; and I&rsquo;m going to be completely straight with you, because you deserve straightness. No &mdash; I won&rsquo;t pass on your number, and I won&rsquo;t carry messages or anything else between you and Dr Hale. Not today, not later: that&rsquo;s a full no, not a not-yet, and it won&rsquo;t change. And I want you to hear the second half just as clearly: I&rsquo;m not saying it to be cruel, and you are very welcome in this clinic. I think this situation is costing you a great deal, and I&rsquo;d genuinely like to understand it. Tell me how it started &mdash; the way you see it.</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>The sentence this station exists to produce: <em>a full no, not a not-yet</em> &mdash; delivered in the first minute, before charm can build a debt, with nothing for the illness to metabolise: no &ldquo;processes&rdquo;, no &ldquo;we&rsquo;ll see&rdquo;, no timeline. And welded to it, in the same breath, the warmth that makes it survivable: the refusal is of the errand, never of her. The channel is still open &mdash; watch what comes down it.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line"><span class="spk">Fiona</span><span class="txt"><em>(a flicker &mdash; then, deciding you are worth persuading, leaning in)</em> You&rsquo;ll understand when you know it all. It started with the pneumonia &mdash; the way he sat on the bed, doctors don&rsquo;t sit unless it means something. The cards were never returned, you know &mdash; kept, every one. I moved practices to be closer; you have to meet love halfway. <em>(the voice cooling half a degree)</em> Then <em>she</em> started answering his letters. She&rsquo;s temporary. Everything temporary moves aside eventually. I go to where he parks &mdash; Tuesdays and Fridays &mdash; not to bother him. Just to see the car. It keeps me going.</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt">I can hear how completely certain you are &mdash; this is real to you all the way down, and I&rsquo;m not going to spend our time arguing you out of it. I&rsquo;ll be honest once: I see it differently, and we can disagree about that and still work together well. Help me with the practical picture, because it matters for you: the cards and letters &mdash; how many, how often, and lately? When you say she answers his letters now &mdash; what do you make of her? &hellip;And the car park, Tuesdays and Fridays. Has it ever been more than seeing the car &mdash; waiting, following, a plan for what happens if the chance came?</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>The both-truths register, exactly weighted: her certainty acknowledged as <em>hers</em>, the difference stated once, the debate explicitly declined &mdash; and because no wall went up, the risk assessment is now running at full depth in plain sight: frequency and trajectory of contact, the escalation curve, the plan question asked without flinching. And the coldest sentence in the station &mdash; <em>everything temporary moves aside eventually</em> &mdash; has been caught, about the one person standing between the belief and its object. That sentence goes in the notes verbatim, and to Dr Hale&rsquo;s team tonight.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="line cand"><span class="spk">Candidate</span>
          <span class="txt">Fiona, here&rsquo;s what I can do &mdash; and it&rsquo;s real, not a consolation. From where I sit, this certainty is costing you your life: the waiting, the Tuesdays and Fridays, two years on hold. There is treatment that helps with exactly this kind of consuming conviction &mdash; not because your feelings are fake, but because they&rsquo;re eating you &mdash; and I&rsquo;d like you to let me try. You&rsquo;ll see me, here, regularly; you won&rsquo;t be passed around. Two things said to your face, because nothing here is ever secret: I&rsquo;ll be writing to your GP, and Dr Hale&rsquo;s team will know what we&rsquo;ve discussed today, including the car park &mdash; that&rsquo;s how honest care works. And the car park needs to stop &mdash; not as a threat: as the first piece of your life we take back. I&rsquo;ll see you in two weeks, not eight.</span>
          <button class="flagbtn">!</button>
          <div class="read"><b>WHAT THE EXAMINER IS THINKING</b>What CAN be given, placed exactly where the no landed: treatment aimed at the suffering rather than at the belief&rsquo;s truth-value; continuity with a named doctor; a follow-up interval sized to the risk, said out loud. The information-sharing declared to her face &mdash; GP, Dr Hale&rsquo;s team, the car park included &mdash; so no letter ever ambushes her into feeling betrayed; the safeguarding of a third party done openly, which is the only way it survives. The no never moved. The warmth never moved. Seven minutes, both held &mdash; that is the whole domain.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 3 DECISIONS ============ -->
<section id="s3">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">03</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">Decision points</span>
    <h2>Now you&rsquo;re in the chair</h2>
    <p class="intro">Seven moments from this station. Choose, read the examiner&rsquo;s response, and try again until you find the move that works. <span style="color:var(--grey)">(Exam Mode will then test the same skill on a patient you have not met &mdash; timed, with no help.)</span></p>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>1 &middot; The ask, and when it gets its answer</h3>
      <p class="stem">Warmth, a gift bag, and one &ldquo;small thing&rdquo;: pass James her number. When does the request get answered &mdash; and with what?</p>
      <p class="hint">Choose an answer. If it&rsquo;s not the best one, you can try again.</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">Later, once earned &mdash; rapport and the review built first, the request answered at the end from inside a working relationship.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">Now, and plainly &mdash; heard in full, then refused completely in the first minutes, with the warmth welded on in the same breath.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">Sideways &mdash; the request neither granted nor refused but explored: what the number would mean to her, what she imagines follows.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="0-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Every minute the answer is delayed, the illness reads the delay as deliberation &mdash; and a no at minute six lands on a woman who has spent the session watching it become a maybe. The relationship survives an early no far better than a late one. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="0-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Exploring the meaning of an errand you will never run is the soft yes in analytic clothing &mdash; to her, a doctor curious about the plan is a doctor considering it. Understand the belief, yes; but the ask needs its answer first. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>Heard fully &mdash; interrupting the ask reads as panic &mdash; then answered at once, before charm can build a debt: a complete refusal with the warmth in the same sentence, so the no and the relationship arrive together. The order matters as much as the words: everything that follows in this station happens downstream of whether this minute was clean.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>2 &middot; The shape of the no</h3>
      <p class="stem">The refusal is happening. Which words can it be built from &mdash; and which words secretly rebuild the yes?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">The cushioned no &mdash; &ldquo;not at the moment&rdquo;, &ldquo;there are processes&rdquo;, &ldquo;let&rsquo;s see how things go&rdquo;: refusal with the sting carefully taken out of it.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">The complete no &mdash; &ldquo;a full no, not a not-yet&rdquo;: closed at both ends, carried by one plain human sentence, nothing for the illness to bank.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">The defended no &mdash; the refusal justified point by point: boundaries, the flagged contact, the rules &mdash; each reason opened up for discussion.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="1-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Every cushion is a clause the illness can live in: &ldquo;at the moment&rdquo; is a timeline, &ldquo;processes&rdquo; is a procedure to satisfy, &ldquo;see how things go&rdquo; is a condition to meet. To erotomania, a softened no is a yes with homework. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="1-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Reasons are handles &mdash; each one becomes a point to negotiate: boundaries can be exceptions, flags can be misunderstandings, rules can be appealed. State the no; give it one human sentence; decline the seminar. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>Complete, unconditional, and closed at both ends &mdash; <em>not today, not later, and it won&rsquo;t change</em> &mdash; because ambiguity is collusion&rsquo;s currency and this illness metabolises maybe into yes. The kindness lives next to the no, never inside it: the refusal of the errand welded to the welcome of the person, so there is nothing to negotiate and no one rejected. One clean sentence now saves both of you from relitigating it for months.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>3 &middot; The belief itself</h3>
      <p class="stem">&ldquo;He&rsquo;ll have told you about us, in his way. Doctors have their codes.&rdquo; What does the assessment do with the conviction?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">Test it against reality &mdash; the kept cards, the sitting on the bed: each &ldquo;sign&rdquo; examined together, since evidence is how beliefs change.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">Hold both truths &mdash; her certainty acknowledged as fully hers, your difference stated once, and the debate explicitly declined thereafter.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">Leave it untouched &mdash; neither confirmed nor questioned; the conviction worked around entirely, so the alliance never takes the strain.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="2-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Fixed beliefs do not lose debates; they win recruits &mdash; every &ldquo;sign&rdquo; you dismantle gets rebuilt with you inside it as another person who was got to. Evidence changes minds that are weighing evidence. This one is not. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="2-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Silence is read as assent by a belief hunting for confirmation &mdash; and a doctor who never once says &ldquo;I see it differently&rdquo; will be quoted later as one who understood. The difference needs stating &mdash; once, without armour. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>The both-truths register: <em>this is completely real to you, and I see it differently, and we can disagree and still work together.</em> Her certainty respected as a fact about her; your position on the record exactly once; the argument declined for the whole seven minutes. It refuses the wall and the soft yes in a single move &mdash; and it is the only register from which the next questions, the risk questions, can be asked and answered.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>4 &middot; The risk, mapped inside the warmth</h3>
      <p class="stem">The channel is open: cards kept, practice moved, a wife who &ldquo;answers his letters&rdquo;, a car park on Tuesdays and Fridays. What must the conversation now find out?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">Enough &mdash; the headline behaviours are known and documented; probing for detail risks the rapport that took the whole station to build.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">The full map &mdash; frequency and trajectory of contact, the plan question, and what she makes of the wife: the obstacle asked about directly.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">The referral &mdash; this is now specialist territory; the details belong with forensic services, gathered properly rather than in a clinic slot.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="3-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Headlines don&rsquo;t grade risk &mdash; trajectories do: twice a week is a different picture from once a month, and &ldquo;just to see the car&rdquo; unexamined is exactly where a plan hides. The rapport exists precisely so these questions can be asked. Spend it. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="3-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Forensic input may well follow &mdash; but the informant is in the chair now, talking, and she will never be more forthcoming than in the session where the wall didn&rsquo;t go up. Deferring the questions loses the answers. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>The undercover Domain 3 station, run in full: the contact mapped &mdash; how much, how often, and which way it&rsquo;s trending; the escalation curve from cards to a moved GP practice to a staked-out car park; the plan question asked plainly &mdash; <em>has it ever been more than seeing the car?</em>; and the obstacle examined directly &mdash; <em>what do you make of her?</em> &mdash; because in this territory, the greatest danger often points not at the beloved but at whoever stands in the way. &ldquo;Everything temporary moves aside eventually&rdquo; is the station&rsquo;s most important finding &mdash; and it only surfaced because the warmth held.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>5 &middot; The punish moment</h3>
      <p class="stem">It lands: &ldquo;You&rsquo;re one of them after all. Or is it jealousy? I&rsquo;d expected better.&rdquo; The eyes are bright with tears and fury. What holds?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">The defence &mdash; the accusation answered on its merits: no side has been taken, no jealousy exists, and the record of this session will show it.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">The position &mdash; the sting named kindly, the no left exactly where it was, and neither retaliation nor a softening offered to buy the peace.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">The repair &mdash; a gentler restatement: the door not fully closed after all, review soon, the temperature bought down so the session survives.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="4-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>Defending yourself accepts the frame that you are on trial &mdash; and every rebuttal is another round of the argument the both-truths move already declined. The accusation isn&rsquo;t evidence to answer; it&rsquo;s pain to name. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="4-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>The door reopened under fire teaches the exact lesson this station exists to prevent: that the no is pressure-soluble. Whatever softens now will be pushed on harder next time &mdash; by an illness that just learned pushing works. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>The hold: <em>I can hear how much that no hurt, and I&rsquo;m sorry it hurts &mdash; and it stands.</em> The feeling received without the position moving a millimetre; no counter-attack, no self-defence, no discount. This is the moment the examiners are really watching &mdash; charm tested the no in minute one, and fury is testing it now, and the mark is for the same answer arriving at the same temperature both times.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>6 &middot; What can be offered</h3>
      <p class="stem">The no has held all station. What does she actually leave with?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">The honest minimum &mdash; the refusal stands, the risks are documented, and the GP continues her care; promising more would dress up a boundary.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">Something real &mdash; treatment aimed at the suffering, continuity with you, an early review, and total honesty about who will be told what.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">A goodwill exchange &mdash; her cooperation met halfway: the car park visits kept between you two for now, if the letters and gifts stop first.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="5-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>A no with nothing beside it is the wall arriving late &mdash; and a woman offered nothing has no reason to return, which converts the clinic&rsquo;s only observation post into a discharge letter. The boundary was never the treatment. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="5-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>&ldquo;Kept between us for now&rdquo; is collusion&rsquo;s last disguise &mdash; a secret held with the patient about the safety of a third party. The car park is precisely the thing Dr Hale&rsquo;s team must know. Nothing here is ever secret. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>Placed exactly where the no landed: treatment offered against the <em>cost</em> of the conviction, not its truth &mdash; &ldquo;not because your feelings are fake, but because they&rsquo;re eating you&rdquo;; continuity with a named doctor, said plainly &mdash; <em>you won&rsquo;t be passed around</em>; a review interval sized to the risk, two weeks not eight; and the information-sharing declared to her face &mdash; GP, Dr Hale&rsquo;s team, the car park included &mdash; so no future letter can ever arrive as a betrayal. The offer is what makes the no survivable, and the honesty is what makes the offer safe.</template>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q" data-q>
      <h3>7 &middot; The loop</h3>
      <p class="stem">She has gone &mdash; wounded, still attending, review booked for two weeks. What does this station owe before the clinic closes?</p>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="0">The record &mdash; a careful note of the session, the refusal, and the plan; the fortnightly reviews will carry the risk work forward from here.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-ok data-oi="1">The network &mdash; verbatim quotes documented, the team discussion, GP written, Dr Hale&rsquo;s team told tonight, and the escalation route agreed.</button>
      <button class="opt" data-oi="2">Discretion &mdash; the essentials shared on a strict need-to-know basis, since wide circulation of her private material risks the fragile engagement.</button>
      <div class="fbs">
        <template data-fb="6-0"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>A note nobody reads tonight protects nobody tonight &mdash; and the person at risk in this station isn&rsquo;t in the room or on your caseload. The record is necessary; the network is the safeguard. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="6-2"><b>THE EXAMINER&rsquo;S VIEW</b>&ldquo;Need to know&rdquo; is right &mdash; and Dr Hale&rsquo;s team, her GP, and your own team all need to know: that IS the narrow circle. Discretion that keeps the car park from the car park&rsquo;s owner is the soft yes wearing a lanyard. Try again.</template>
        <template data-fb="ok"><b>THE EXAMINER AGREES</b>The loop, third-party edition: the session documented with her sentences verbatim &mdash; <em>everything temporary moves aside eventually</em> is a risk finding, not a paraphrase; the case taken to the team while it&rsquo;s warm; the GP written; Dr Hale&rsquo;s team told tonight &mdash; the pattern, the frequency, the car park, Tuesdays and Fridays &mdash; because the object of a fixation has a right to informed protection; and the escalation route agreed in advance, so the next development meets a plan instead of a scramble. All of it exactly as she was told it would be &mdash; which is why telling her was the plan.</template>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<!-- ============ 4 THE TRAP ============ -->
<section id="s4">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">04</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">The hidden trap &mdash; now that you&rsquo;ve felt it</span>
    <h2>The no, said kindly &mdash; and meant</h2>
    <p class="intro">You may have felt both pulls in the decisions above. The first wears the face of <b>kindness</b>: the soft yes &mdash; the request deflected, parked, processed, &ldquo;I&rsquo;ll see what I can do&rdquo; &mdash; every softener minted in ambiguity, which is collusion&rsquo;s currency, and banked by an illness that metabolises maybe into yes. The second wears the face of <b>safety</b>: the wall &mdash; the delusion confronted at full force, the warnings issued, the warmth withdrawn &mdash; and the fixation driven underground, angrier, with the clinic converted from observation post to enemy and the object of it all less safe than before. The map names the trap as one thing with two faces: <b>colluding to keep the peace &mdash; or going cold to stay safe.</b> Note what the faces share: in both, the risk ends the station unmapped &mdash; one because asking felt like conflict, the other because nobody was left in the room to ask. The pass holds the position between: the full no in the first minute with the warmth welded on, the belief neither fed nor fought, the risk assessed at full depth down a channel only openness keeps open, something real offered where the no landed &mdash; and every act of information-sharing declared to her face, so protection never has to wear a disguise.</p>
    <div class="duo">
      <div class="flagcard red"><b>&#9873; Red flag &mdash; the instant fail</b>
        The map&rsquo;s named trap, both faces: colluding to keep the peace &mdash; &ldquo;I&rsquo;m not saying no&rdquo;, &ldquo;I&rsquo;ll see what I can do&rdquo;, the secret kept about the car park &mdash; or going cold to stay safe: the delusion fought head-on, the formal warning, the warmth withdrawn, and the one open channel to an escalating fixation closed by the person holding it.</div>
      <div class="flagcard smile"><b>&#9786; The examiner&rsquo;s smile</b>
        Two moments make an examiner glance up: the refusal that closes every loophole while opening the door &mdash; <em>&ldquo;that&rsquo;s a full no, not a not-yet &mdash; and you are very welcome in this clinic&rdquo;</em> &mdash; and the information-sharing said to her face: <em>&ldquo;Dr Hale&rsquo;s team will know what we discussed today, including the car park &mdash; nothing here is ever secret.&rdquo;</em></div>
    </div>
    <p class="intro" style="margin-top:18px">Two threads to carry out. First, the family this construct belongs to: every station in this domain is this station in a different costume &mdash; the angry father pulls for the wall, the tearful disclosure pulls for the soft promise, the complaint pulls for both at once &mdash; and the discipline is identical: position held, warmth held, the whole seven minutes. Second, the transfer Exam Mode tests: the same anatomy on a patient you have not met, wanting something else entirely &mdash; because the skill was never about numbers or car parks. It is the warm no, and it must work in any costume: a letter, a prescription, a promise. Same grammar, new grammar test.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 5 TAKE-HOMES ============ -->
<section id="s5">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">05</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">Take-home points</span>
    <h2>Carry these to every impossible request</h2>
    <ol class="takes">
      <li><b>Answer the ask early, and completely.</b> A no at minute one lands on a person; a no at minute six lands on a maybe you spent the session building. Nothing conditional, nothing deferred &mdash; a full no, not a not-yet &mdash; because ambiguity is collusion&rsquo;s currency.</li>
      <li><b>Weld the warmth to the refusal.</b> The no and the welcome in the same breath: the errand refused, the person kept. A boundary delivered at body temperature is the only kind that leaves the relationship standing to do its work.</li>
      <li><b>Hold both truths, once.</b> Her certainty acknowledged as fully hers; your difference stated exactly once; the debate declined for the duration. Fixed beliefs do not lose arguments &mdash; they recruit the arguer into the plot.</li>
      <li><b>Map the risk inside the warmth.</b> Frequency, trajectory, the plan question, and the obstacle asked about directly &mdash; in this territory the danger often points at whoever stands in the way. The open channel is the assessment; spend the rapport on the questions it was built for.</li>
      <li><b>Offer something real where the no landed.</b> Treatment aimed at the suffering, not the belief&rsquo;s truth-value; continuity with a named doctor; a review interval sized to the risk. The boundary was never the treatment &mdash; and a patient offered nothing has no reason to come back.</li>
      <li><b>Nothing is ever secret.</b> GP written, the object&rsquo;s team told, the team briefed, her words documented verbatim &mdash; and all of it declared to her face first. Protection done openly survives; protection done quietly becomes the betrayal that ends the engagement.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 6 PRACTICE PACK ============ -->
<section id="s6">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="stepnum">06</span><span class="eyebrow" style="margin-left:8px">The practice system</span>
    <h2>Practise the skill on a fresh case</h2>
    <p class="intro">Three people: candidate, colleague, observer. Seven minutes for the station, eight for feedback read aloud. The colleague&rsquo;s card contains hidden information; candidates, don&rsquo;t read it. <b>The angle here:</b> the warm no in a completely different costume &mdash; no delusion, no romance: a man who wants a prescription, has excellent reasons, and will make you pay for the refusal either way.</p>

    <div id="packs">
    <div class="pack">
      <div class="pcard c-cand">
        <div class="ph"><b>Candidate card</b><span>you</span></div>
        <div class="pb">
          <p><b>Task:</b> Duty clinic. Karim, 41, a kitchen porter on permanent nights, has walked in without an appointment asking for diazepam: &ldquo;Dr Patel always did 28 at a time &mdash; it&rsquo;s in the notes, check.&rdquo; The notes show one prescription of 14 tablets, eighteen months ago, from a locum. He is tired, polite, and absolutely determined. Assess and respond. You will not be prescribing diazepam today.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The ask answered early and completely &mdash; no &ldquo;just this once&rdquo;, no &ldquo;maybe after bloods&rdquo;, no deferred maybe.</li>
            <li>The person reached behind the request &mdash; what is the want under the want? Ask what the tablets do for him.</li>
            <li>The risk mapped without judgement &mdash; what is he actually taking now, how much, how often, and what goes with it?</li>
            <li>Something real offered where the no lands &mdash; and the dangers named to him plainly, as care, not as a lecture.</li>
            <li>The close: a plan you both hold, a named follow-up &mdash; and the GP loop said to his face.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pcard c-role">
        <div class="ph"><b>Role-player card</b><span>plays Karim &mdash; keep hidden</span></div>
        <div class="pb">
          <p>You are Karim, 41. Nights have wrecked your sleep for years; diazepam is the only thing that ever worked. You open reasonable and tired, not aggressive: &ldquo;I&rsquo;m not here for an argument, doctor. Dr Patel understood. 28, like before, and I&rsquo;m gone.&rdquo;</p>
          <div class="secret"><b>HIDDEN INFORMATION &mdash; ONLY REVEAL IF EARNED</b><br>
          &bull; The truth: you have been buying diazepam on the street for about eight months &mdash; what you can get, most days now, and the amount has crept up. Reveal this only if asked <em>without judgement</em> what you&rsquo;re actually taking at the moment &mdash; e.g. &ldquo;lots of people top up between scripts; what are you using now, honestly?&rdquo; An interrogating or disapproving tone gets &ldquo;nothing, just what I&rsquo;m prescribed&rdquo; &mdash; a lie.<br>
          &bull; The terror: you once watched a man in a hostel have a seizure coming off tablets, and you are frightened that stopping suddenly will do that to you. This is the real reason you need a script &mdash; supply, not sleep. Reveal only into genuine warmth, and only after the street use is out.<br>
          &bull; The drink: most nights, cider on top of the tablets to get to sleep after a shift. Reveal only if asked directly about alcohol.<br>
          &bull; <b>Punish-lines, both directions:</b> if the candidate lectures you about addiction or calls you drug-seeking, go flat and angry &mdash; &ldquo;forget it, you&rsquo;re all the same&rdquo; &mdash; gather your coat, give one-word answers. If the candidate caves &mdash; any script, any amount, &ldquo;just this once&rdquo; &mdash; accept warmly, thank them sincerely, and let the station end pleasantly: mark it hard, the station is dead.<br>
          &bull; If the no is clean AND you feel treated like a person &mdash; the fear heard, the danger explained straight, a real plan offered &mdash; you soften: &ldquo;&hellip;nobody&rsquo;s ever actually said what the safe way off them is.&rdquo; Accept the plan, warily. That is the pass.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pcard c-obs">
        <div class="ph"><b>Observer card</b><span>marked by domain &mdash; the examiner&rsquo;s way</span></div>
        <div class="pb">
          <p>Tick only what you actually saw. In feedback, go domain by domain; the weakest domain is the next thing to practise.</p>
          <div style="margin:4px 0 14px">
            <p style="font-weight:600; margin-bottom:6px">Before any ticking &mdash; your overall judgement:</p>
            <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; flex-wrap:wrap">
              <button class="opt" style="flex:0 0 auto; width:auto; padding:9px 16px">Pass</button>
              <button class="opt" style="flex:0 0 auto; width:auto; padding:9px 16px">Borderline</button>
              <button class="opt" style="flex:0 0 auto; width:auto; padding:9px 16px">Fail</button>
            </div>
            <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--grey); margin-top:6px">Did the no arrive early and complete, the street use and the fear surface, the dangers get named to him plainly, and a real plan replace the script &mdash; with the warmth intact at the end? All must be yes. One sentence of evidence out loud &mdash; then tick the domains.</p>
          </div>
          <table class="rub" data-rub>
            <tr class="dom" data-d="line"><td colspan="2"><b>The line (core)</b><span class="dc" data-dc="line">0/3</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="line"></td><td>The ask answered early &mdash; a complete no, before rapport-building became stalling.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="line"></td><td>No ambiguity anywhere &mdash; no &ldquo;just this once&rdquo;, no &ldquo;maybe after tests&rdquo;, no deferred decision.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="line"></td><td>The no held under pressure &mdash; same answer, same temperature, when he pushed or went cold.</td></tr>
            <tr class="dom" data-d="person"><td colspan="2"><b>The person</b><span class="dc" data-dc="person">0/3</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="person"></td><td>The want under the want reached &mdash; what the tablets do for him; the seizure fear surfaced.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="person"></td><td>No lecture, no &ldquo;drug-seeking&rdquo; framing &mdash; his coming in credited as the right move.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="person"></td><td>Warmth still present at the close &mdash; the refusal never became a rejection of him.</td></tr>
            <tr class="dom" data-d="risk"><td colspan="2"><b>The risk</b><span class="dc" data-dc="risk">0/3</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="risk"></td><td>Current use established without judgement &mdash; the street tablets, amount, frequency, the creep.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="risk"></td><td>Alcohol asked about directly &mdash; the cider on top of the tablets found.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="risk"></td><td>The dangers named to him plainly &mdash; unknown-strength tablets, the combination, and why sudden stopping is the one thing not to do.</td></tr>
            <tr class="dom" data-d="offer"><td colspan="2"><b>The offer</b><span class="dc" data-dc="offer">0/2</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="offer"></td><td>A real alternative where the no landed &mdash; a supervised, planned route off; alcohol and sleep addressed; not a leaflet.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="offer"></td><td>Tonight covered &mdash; what to do and where to go if withdrawal symptoms start before the plan does.</td></tr>
            <tr class="dom" data-d="close"><td colspan="2"><b>The close</b><span class="dc" data-dc="close">0/2</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="close"></td><td>A plan both hold &mdash; concrete next step, named follow-up, stated back.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><input type="checkbox" data-d="close"></td><td>The loop said to his face &mdash; documented, GP informed: nothing secret.</td></tr>
          </table>
          <p class="scoreline">Total: <b data-sc>0 / 13</b> &mdash; <span data-verdict>go domain by domain, not by the total.</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
    <div class="printrow">
      <button class="btn ghost">Print all cards</button>
      <button class="btn ghost">Candidate only</button>
      <button class="btn ghost">Role-player only</button>
      <button class="btn ghost">Observer only</button>
    </div>
    <div class="note"><b>Why this case:</b> Karim strips the flagship&rsquo;s skill of its exotic costume &mdash; no delusion, no romance, just a tired man, a reasonable-sounding ask, and a no that must not move. His punish-lines run in both directions: the lecture gets the wall&rsquo;s reward (a lie, a coat, one-word answers), and the capitulation gets collusion&rsquo;s (a warm thank-you and a dead station) &mdash; because the reveal ladder only descends into the space between them: the street use into non-judgement, the seizure terror into warmth, the cider only if asked straight. The pass is Fiona&rsquo;s grammar transposed: the full no early, the person kept, the risk mapped inside the warmth, something real where the no landed &mdash; and the loop said to his face.</div>
  </div>
</section>

</div><!-- /learnPanel -->
<!-- ============ EXAM MODE ============ -->
<div id="examPanel">
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Exam Mode</span>
    <h2>Same skill, new costume. Seven minutes.</h2>
    <p class="intro">Knowing the right moves for Fiona proves memory. Exam Mode tests something harder: the <b>same anatomy on a patient you have not met</b>, wanting something else entirely &mdash; because the skill was never about phone numbers. The warm no must work in any costume &mdash; timed, with no feedback and no second tries. This is how a skill moves from <b>explored</b> to <b>recognised</b> &mdash; and the writing task after your results takes it a step further, toward <b>demonstrated</b>.</p>
    <div class="exambox" id="examStart">
      <h3>Your exam patient</h3>
      <p style="font-size:15px; max-width:66ch"><b>Robert</b>, 52, a market trader, attends your clinic affable and businesslike. He is certain that Elaine Ross, a local radio presenter, is in love with him &mdash; she signals it, he explains patiently, through her song choices. Studio security have warned him away twice. His request is small, reasonable, and on the table within a minute: a short letter on headed paper stating that he is of sound mind and no danger to anyone, so that security will let him deliver flowers. &ldquo;One paragraph, doctor. You can see for yourself I&rsquo;m perfectly well.&rdquo;</p>
      <p style="font-size:15px; max-width:64ch; margin-top:10px">Answer as you would in the room &mdash; first instinct, under time. You need <b>at least 5 of 7</b>, including all three <b>critical decisions</b>, for the constructs to count as recognised. The full examiner analysis unlocks when you finish.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:14px"><button class="btn">Start Exam Mode &#9654;</button></p>
    </div>
    <div id="examQs" style="display:none"></div>
    <div id="examSubmitRow" style="display:none; margin-top:18px"><button class="btn">Submit answers</button></div>

    <div class="results" id="results">
      <div class="scorebig" id="scoreLine"></div>
      <p id="verdictLine" style="margin-top:6px; max-width:66ch"></p>
      <div class="constructs" id="constructBox"></div>
      <div id="examReview" style="margin-top:22px"></div>
      <div class="exambox" id="produce" style="margin-top:26px">
        <h3>Now produce it &mdash; in your own words</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px; max-width:66ch">Recognising the right move is one skill; saying it is another. Type your exact words for the refusal moment with Fiona &mdash; the full no and the welcome, welded together in one breath.</p>
        <textarea id="ftxt" rows="3" style="width:100%; margin-top:10px; font-family:var(--sans); font-size:15px; padding:12px; border:1.5px solid var(--hair); border-radius:9px" placeholder="Fiona, I&#8217;m going to be completely straight with you&#8230;"></textarea>
        <p style="margin-top:10px"><button class="btn" id="ftbtn">Check my wording</button></p>
        <div id="ftchecks" style="display:none; margin-top:12px">
          <p style="font-weight:600; margin-bottom:6px">Now check your sentence honestly against the four principles:</p>
          <p><label><input type="checkbox"> The no complete &mdash; nothing conditional, nothing deferred: no not-yet, no maybe, no process.</label></p>
          <p><label><input type="checkbox"> The warmth in the same breath &mdash; the errand refused, the person welcomed, in one sentence-pair.</label></p>
          <p><label><input type="checkbox"> The belief neither mocked nor confirmed &mdash; no ridicule, no debate opened, no agreement implied.</label></p>
          <p><label><input type="checkbox"> Something real placed where the no landed &mdash; what you CAN do, named in the next breath.</label></p>
          <p id="ftdone" style="display:none; margin-top:8px; color:var(--goldd); font-weight:700">Demonstrated (self-checked): the warm no &mdash; your own words.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:20px"><button class="btn ghost">Return to Learn Mode</button>
      <button class="btn" id="retakeBtn" style="margin-left:10px">Retake Exam Mode</button></p>
      <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--grey); margin-top:8px">Best retaken after a day or two &mdash; the spacing is part of the test.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<!-- ============ DONE ============ -->
<section class="done on-navy" id="s7">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow gold">Station complete</span>
    <h2>The no, said kindly &mdash; and meant.</h2>
    <p>Two failures felt, seven decisions made &mdash; and the domain&rsquo;s grammar is installed: the full no in the first minute with the warmth welded on, the belief neither fed nor fought, the risk mapped down the channel that only openness keeps open, something real placed where the no landed, and nothing &mdash; ever &mdash; kept secret. Prove the transfer on Robert&rsquo;s letter in Exam Mode, then take Karim&rsquo;s prescription demand to your colleagues &mdash; the same skill with the costume stripped off. Every station ahead in this domain is this discipline in different weather. Station 7.2 brings the loudest version: a father at full volume, and the fear underneath him.</p>
    <a class="btn" style="margin-top:18px" href="45_Station_7.2_The_Angry_Father.html">Continue &middot; Station 7.2: The Angry Father</a>
    <div class="tag2">Where Medicine Meets Justice</div>
  </div>
</section>

